      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-21-pcapanalyzer-self-hosted-pcap-analyzer-with-27-problem-detec",
      "title": "PcapAnalyzer – self-hosted pcap analyzer with 27 problem detectors",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/sebaandrada-cell/PcapAnalyzer\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50594132\nPoints: 84\n# Comments: 9",
      "body": "Find the network fault in seconds, not hours. Upload a .pcap / .pcapng capture\n(gzip too) and PcapAnalyzer tells you what is failing, why, and what to check next.\nIt runs on your own machine, so captures never leave your network.\nFree and open source (Apache 2.0). Status: beta.\nTry it without installing anything: https://pcap-analyzer-seven.vercel.app/#demo\nDownload: https://sebaandrada6.gumroad.com/l/hspgx (free) or clone this repository.\n27 detectors that run on every capture, each with a severity and a next step:\nTCP: firewall blocks (SYN→RST), retransmissions, duplicate ACKs, loss and\nreordering, zero and full windows, resets after the handshake, slow handshakes.\nPath: PMTUD black holes, low MSS, IP fragmentation, ICMP errors, routing loops.\nName and address services: unanswered or slow DNS, SERVFAIL, NXDOMAIN bursts,\nDHCP NAK / DECLINE / no answer, duplicate IPs, ARP storms.\nApplications: HTTP 4xx / 5xx and slow responses, TLS alerts, SSL 3.0 / TLS 1.0 / 1.1.\nTunnels: IPsec (IKE and ESP), WireGuard, OpenVPN, GRE, L2TP and Teredo that are\none-way, never answer a handshake or keep renegotiating.\nSecurity: port scans and sweeps, cleartext logins (FTP, POP3, IMAP, SMTP AUTH,\nHTTP Basic; credentials are never stored or shown), Telnet / SMBv1 / SNMP v1-v2c,\nARP spoofing, overlapping IP fragments.\nCapture quality first. It warns when the capture itself limits the result:\nframes duplicated by a mirror port, traffic seen in one direction only, truncated\npackets, connections already open when the capture started.\nWireshark-style views: packet list with real Wireshark display filters over the\nwhole capture, colouring, CSV export, expert info, HTTP / DNS / DHCP / TLS tables,\nresponse times and a flow diagram per conversation.\nAI investigation (optional): an AI investigates the capture with tools (real\nfilters, stream detail, statistics) and cites the packets behind every claim. You\ncan then ask follow-up questions. It uses your own Anthropic API key; without one, a\ndemo mode runs the full flow with text generated from the analysis, at no cost.\nPDF report, Spanish and English interface, light and dark theme.\nYou need Docker with Docker Compose. On Windows, run the script from Git Bash or WSL.\nThe script creates a random access token (shown once, stored in .env) and starts the\napp. When the build finishes, open http://localhost:8080, paste the token into the\n\"API token\" field (top right) and upload a capture, or click \"Try the sample capture\".\nThe app listens on 127.0.0.1 only. Do not expose it on a network without an\nauthenticated reverse proxy: the API can use your AI account.\nQUICKSTART.md has the details, the AI setup and troubleshooting.\nYou need Python 3.9+, Node 20+ and tshark (installed with Wireshark).\nexport API_TOKENS=\"$(openssl rand -hex 32)\"\nOpen http://localhost:5173 and paste the same token. If tshark is not on your PATH,\nset TSHARK_PATH to the binary.\nThe capture is analysed on your machine. While an AI investigation lasts it is kept\nencrypted (60 minutes of inactivity, or until you press \"Delete capture now\") and is\nThe AI is optional. It only sees what its tools return (packet metadata; packet\ncontent only if you switch it on for that session), never the pcap file.\nNo telemetry and no accounts for the self-hosted version.\ncd backend && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q    # needs tshark\ncd frontend && npm test\nPcapAnalyzer is a beta. It has been tested with synthetic fixtures and public sample\ncaptures, and the most useful feedback is a capture where it misses a problem or\nreports one that is not real. Please open an issue at\nhttps://github.com/sebaandrada-cell/PcapAnalyzer/issues and describe the case.\nDo not attach captures that contain real credentials or customer data; anonymise\nthem first or describe the pattern.\nThe technical reference (JSON schema, detector thresholds, limits, API errors) is in\nApache License 2.0. See NOTICE for third-party software: tshark /\nWireshark (GPL) runs as a separate program and is not distributed with PcapAnalyzer.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
