      "id": "bbc-2026-11-21-uk-should-only-rejoin-eu-if-it-innovates-on-technology-blair",
      "title": "UK should only rejoin EU if it innovates on technology, Blair warns",
      "summary": "The former prime minister argues the European Union is probably moving in the wrong direction on technology innovation.",
      "body": "Former prime minister Sir Tony Blair has said Britain should only rejoin the European Union if it reforms - and allows more innovation on technology.Speaking to The Sunday Times, external, Sir Tony said: \"I was painted as saying Britain should just go back and rejoin - I'm not saying that - it's heavily conditioned.\"Sir Tony was a prominent opponent of leaving the EU, and told the paper: \"I do think Brexit was a real mistake.\"But he added the debate was different now than it was in 2016. Referencing the need for technology innovation, he said Europe could and \"probably are\" moving in the wrong direction.He said: \"The problem if we go back and join Europe is that; I can't say that the technology revolution is the single biggest thing, and then if Europe moves in the wrong direction on technology innovation, which they might do and presently probably are doing, that it's a good idea for Britain to rejoin. That's what's changed in this last ten years.\"He argued Britain should have an ambition to reform the EU.But he added that we have to be \"prepared to walk away from that negotiation\" and need to make our own economy and tech sector strong. Prime Minister Andy Burnham this week agreed what he called a \"win-win\" deal with the EU.The agreement covered British food exports, emissions trading and a youth experience scheme.European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen also announced that the trading bloc and the UK are launching a digital partnership, including areas like artificial intelligence (AI) and quantum technology.The EU and Britain \"have enormous potential to innovate together\", she added.",
      "source": "BBC",
