      "id": "bbc-2026-11-21-sessions-offer-advice-on-rising-energy-costs",
      "title": "Sessions offer advice on rising energy costs",
      "summary": "A council is urging people to seek support with rising energy costs on heating this winter.",
      "body": "Nora Corkery, chief executive of Devon Communities Together, said: \"Behind every statistic is a household making difficult choices: rationing the heating, putting off filling up a tank, or cutting back on journeys they can't really do without.\"The charity said people could access confidential one-to-one support to find financial help, with a limited number of free winter warm packs available for those who attend.Cheryl Cottle-Hunkin, from Devon County Council, said: \"I'd urge anyone who is struggling, or worried about the winter ahead, to seek advice and find out what help may be available.\"More information on the sessions was available on the charity's website, external.Follow BBC Devon on X, external, Facebook, external and Instagram, external. Send your story ideas to spotlight@bbc.co.uk, external.",
