    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-20-nfl-great-brady-could-buy-chelsea-stake",
      "title": "NFL great Brady could buy Chelsea stake",
      "summary": "American football great Tom Brady is looking to invest in Chelsea through ownership group Clearlake Capital.",
      "body": "American football great Tom Brady is looking to invest in Chelsea through ownership group Clearlake Capital.The seven-time Super Bowl winner has recently divested his stake in Championship club Birmingham City, which he bought into following Tom Wagner's Knighthead Capital takeover in 2023.It now appears he could move into Chelsea, where he has a positive relationship with influential co-owner Behdad Eghbali, having been a star guest at the after-party following the club's Club World Cup triumph in 2025.Brady would have no voting rights or control at Chelsea, although the ownership group could look to appoint him to the board if it suited all parties.The move is not said to be linked to Todd Boehly and Mark Walter's £950m sale of their stakes to Clearlake Capital, which must be completed by the end of the year.Meanwhile, Swiss billionaire Hansjorg Wyss remains a significant minority stakeholder at Stamford Bridge.The investment is also not part of a funding round, according to senior sources, and is not intended to dilute Clearlake Capital's control.However, other interested parties are said to have approached them about investing since Boehly and Walter agreed a deal to leave.Former quarterback Brady, a three-time NFL most valuable player, retired in February 2023 after 23 seasons in the NFL, having won six Super Bowl rings with the New England Patriots and one with the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.Following the end of his playing career he acquired a stake in the Las Vegas Raiders, while also becoming part of the ownership group of the WNBA's Las Vegas Aces.On top of that, Brady's commitments include him being a lead NFL analyst for Fox Sports.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
