      "id": "bbc-2026-11-20-gb-s-davis-cup-winning-captain-ends-17-year-stint",
      "title": "GB's Davis Cup-winning captain ends 17-year stint",
      "summary": "Leon Smith says helping Britain end a 79-year wait to win the Davis Cup is \"one of the proudest moments\" of his career.",
      "body": "Great Britain's Davis Cup-winning captain Leon Smith is stepping down after almost 17 years in the role.Smith guided the British men's team to Davis Cup victory in 2015 - the nation's first win in the event since 1936.The 50-year-old Scot will leave his role after next week's Finals in Bologna, where he is hoping to create \"another special memory\" by leading the team to the title once again.Smith's successor has not yet been appointed, but the Lawn Tennis Association (LTA) has spoken to potential candidates and hopes to announce the new captain as soon as possible.Former world number one Andy Murray, who was instrumental in Britain's 2015 triumph, is not believed to be interested in the role at this time.\"It has been an enormous privilege to lead the team for so many years, and I feel now is the right time, both for me personally and for the team moving forwards,\" Smith said.\"Winning the Davis Cup in 2015 will always be one of the proudest moments of my career, but there are countless other experiences and memories that I'll cherish forever.\"With Smith picking the team and creating a tight bond between the group, Murray was the driving force on the court as he won all eight of his singles matches in the victorious campaign.Murray was coached by Smith as a child and said winning the Davis Cup together was \"one of the proudest moments\" of his career. \"He did a great job of bringing everyone together and making sure we all felt we had a part to play. He got the best out of us that year,\" three-time Grand Slam champion Murray said.\"I've obviously known Leon a long time, I think the most fun we had together was when I was playing Davis Cup and Leon was on the bench. I'm really glad we got to share those moments. \"I wish Leon all the best as he steps down, and good luck to the new captain.\"Smith, who will continue in his role as head of British men's tennis, took over in 2010 with the team in danger of being relegated to the lowest tier of the Davis Cup.Within three years they were back in the top tier and just two years later Murray inspired them to the trophy.Smith also guided the team to the semi-finals in 2016 and 2019.While he can no longer rely on a superstar of Murray's ilk, Smith is hoping this year's crop can ensure his captaincy ends on another high.Britain will rely on Wimbledon semi-finalist Arthur Fery and former world number eight Cameron Norrie in the singles, with world number one Henry Patten and three-time major champion Neal Skupski pairing up in the doubles.Smith's side faces Germany - led by singles world number one Alexander Zverev - in the last eight on Thursday.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
