      "id": "bbc-2026-11-20-tinned-food-and-long-life-milk-boost-retail-sales-after-be-r",
      "title": "Tinned food and long-life milk boost retail sales after 'Be Ready' campaign launch",
      "summary": "People stocking up on long-life food drove retail sales higher October, according to official data.",
      "body": "Retail sales rose in October, driven by people buying long-life food such as tinned goods and UHT milk, according to official figures.Sales volumes were 0.7% higher as people responded to the government's emergency preparedness \"Be Ready\" campaign, the Office for National Statistics (ONS) said.The campaign encouraged people to stock up in case of disruption to essential services by severe weather or cyberattacks.Separate research released last week suggested that while households were stockpiling essentials, they were not panic buying.The government campaign encouraged people to keep three days' worth of food and water in their homes.Wet wipes, a torch and cash were also recommended.Data from retail research firm Worldpanel by Numerator indicated last week that  people were stocking up on items including tinned meat, bottled water and hand sanitiser.The latest official sales figures, external from the ONS add to the evidence that the public has begun stockpiling.\"Supermarkets have told us that sales of long-life food items such as tinned food and UHT milk were boosted by the government's 'Be Ready' campaign,\" ONS chief economist Grant Fitzner said.\"Meanwhile fuel sales have been recovering from earlier low levels, despite pump prices rising again.\"The rise in retail sales last month beat some economists' expectations - they had predicted a slight fall - and the increase came after a 0.6% decline in September.As well as sales being boosted by people buying essentials, visits to art galleries and clothing purchases were also higher in October.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T09:44:56.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/b2f3/live/616b7460-e4bd-11f1-bd65-4bcf15946188.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck053mzy2qqeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
