      "id": "theverge-2026-11-19-the-analogue-3d-can-now-update-itself-over-wi-fi",
      "title": "The Analogue 3D can now update itself over Wi-Fi",
      "summary": "Analogue has long been good at expanding the features and functionality of its consoles through regular firmware updates, but installing those updates has always required moving files around with a memory card. That's no longer the case with the Analogue 3D, the company's modernized version of the Nintendo 64. Although the console has had Wi-Fi hardware since day one, it's only now been finally ac",
      "body": "Analogue has long been good at expanding the features and functionality of its consoles through regular firmware updates, but installing those updates has always required moving files around with a memory card. That’s no longer the case with the Analogue 3D, the company’s modernized version of the Nintendo 64. Although the console has had Wi-Fi hardware since day one, it’s only now been finally activated through the last update you’ll need to install with a memory card.\nAnalogue released the version 1.6.0 firmware for the Analogue 3D yesterday which adds support for 2.4GHz, 5GHz, mixed, and hidden Wi-Fi networks. Once the update is installed the Wi-Fi setup process will begin automatically when the console is booted, but there’s now an added Wi-Fi section in the Analogue 3D’s settings menu for updating passwords and other details later.\nThe console’s new Wi-Fi capabilities add a couple of useful features at launch. In the future the Analogue 3D will be able to download and install firmware updates so it automatically keeps itself up to date. The new wireless capabilities enable automatic date and time settings based on your time zone, too, and in the privacy section of the console’s settings menu you’ll now find an option for sharing “anonymous usage and analytics data” with Analogue to help further improve its hardware.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gadgets",
        "Gaming",
        "News",
        "Tech"
      ],
      "author": "Andrew Liszewski",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T14:32:33.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/08/257891_Analogue_3D_AKrales_0002.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.732984293194,100,78.534031413613",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/tech/1037552/analogue-3d-nintendo-64-console-wi-fi-activated-automatic-updates",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
