      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-19-php-8-5-13",
      "title": "PHP 8.5.13",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.php.net/ChangeLog-8.php\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50560334\nPoints: 25\n# Comments: 12",
      "body": "8.6 | 8.5 | 8.4 | 8.3 | 8.2 | 8.1 | 8.0\nFix potential ABI incompatibility when adding fields in patches by adding padding to globals.\nFix function and constant imports in compile_to_ast and add support for grouping.\nFixed bug GH-24668 (zend_set_local_var() leaks the previous value of an existing CV).\nFixed unmapping of an unrelated range when the aligned chunk mmap fails (Marti2203).\nFixed bug GH-25023 (ZEND_CONTAINER_OF() fails to compile with -std=c11).\nFixed AST printing dropping final on class constants and properties, and abstract on properties.\nFixed AST export of readonly anonymous classes dropping the readonly modifier.\nFixed memory leak of a duplicate named argument in new in initializer.\nFixed bug GH-25061 ($x = $x - 1 on null is optimized to PRE_DEC).\nFixed first-class callables to static methods in trait constant expressions resolving to the method of the first using class and bypassing visibility checks.\nFixed bug GH-24184 (System ID not being reinitialized after an Apache graceful restart, potentially causing incompatible OPcache file cache entries to be reused).\nFixed memory leak when an exception already contains the pending exception in its previous chain.\nFixed bug GH-23979 (Nullsafe operator must not flush delayed oplines of an enclosing function).\nFixed memory manager keeping a block reallocated to exactly the size of the next smaller bin in its larger bin, which efree_size() then freed into the wrong one.\nFix throwing behaviour with recursive arrays in VM.\nFixed skipped catch block when switching fibers during exception unwinding (Nicolas Grekas)\nFix escape analysis for objects implementing ArrayAccess.\nFixed GH-23921 (Fibers start with error_reporting = 0 when the error_reporting INI directive is not set).\nDeprecated using \"let\" or \"is\" as the name of a class, function, or constant, and as an alias in class_alias() and use declarations.\nDeprecated using \"_\" as a constant name and as an alias for a class or constant in use declarations.\nFixed incorrect internal pointer and foreach iterator positions when compacting arrays with holes.\nFix handling of references to typed properties during unserialization of various internal classes.\nFixed bug GH-23752 (Use scoped diagnostic suppression for the global register declarations so the caller's -Wvolatile-register-var state is restored).\nFixed OSS-Fuzz #538730793 (Assertion failure when returning by-ref from closure invoke).\nFixed OSS-Fuzz #540904105 (ASSERT: ast->attr == T_CLASS_C).\nCalling is_a() or is_subclass_of() with a string as the first argument when $allow_string is false is now deprecated.\nEnabled the TAILCALL VM (--disable-gcc-global-regs) when building with GCC >= 16.\nFixed GH-10497 (Allow direct mutation of objects stored in constants or class constants via OBJ->prop = $val).\nUsing the return statement in a finally block is now deprecated.\nDeprecated \"namespace\" as a class constant name.\nChanged run-tests.php to run in parallel by default, using up to 10 automatically detected workers. Pass -j1 for sequential execution.\nAllowed readonly properties to declare default values.\nChanged run-tests.php to run test subprocesses without a shell where possible.\nFixed GH-23121 (is_callable() wrongly accepts objects with no get_closure handler).\nPassing a 3rd argument to define() is now deprecated.\nNaming a function readonly is now deprecated.\nImplemented partial function application RFC.\nCompile array_map() into a foreach() loop when using Partial Function Application as callback.\nFixed bug GH-22263 (reset typed property default on every unserialize failure path).\nFixed bug GH-18847 (SEGV in zend_fetch_debug_backtrace() when the memory limit is reached while the tracing JIT enters a call frame).\nSync Boost.Context assembly with 1.91.0.\nFixed bug GH-22387 (AST pretty-printing drops meaningful parentheses around RHS of instanceof).\nFixed bug GH-15672 and GH-15911 (Stack overflow when an internal function recurses through zend_call_function, such as a self-attached SPL iterator).\nabort() instead of exit() on hard OOM.\nperf: ZTS: move AG and SCNG into native __thread storage.\nAdded first-class callable cache to share instances for the duration of the request.\nIt is now possible to use reference assign on WeakMap without the key needing to be present beforehand.\nFix OSS-Fuzz #429429090 (Failed assertion on unset() with uninitialized container).\nFixed GH-20564 (Don't call autoloaders with pending exception).\nFixed bug GH-20174 (Assertion failure in ReflectionProperty::skipLazyInitialization after failed LazyProxy initialization).\nEnabled the TAILCALL VM on Windows when compiling with Clang >= 19 x86_64.\nDeprecate specifying a nullable return type for __debugInfo().\nFixed bug GH-22046 (The unserialize function can lead to segfault when non-Serializable internal classes are serialized back with the C format).\nFixed bug GH-22292 (AST pretty printing does not correctly handle invalid variable names).\nFixed bug GH-22291 (AST pretty printing does not correctly handle braces in string interpolation).\nFixed bug GH-22373 (AST pretty-printing drops meaningful parentheses surrounding property access).\nFixed GH-22422 (zend_arena layout mismatch leaked memory in separately built extensions under AddressSanitizer).\nTSRM: use local-exec TLS in PIE executables.\nperf: make all static extensions use TSRMG_STATIC.\nFixed bug GH-22257 (type confusion in Exception::getTraceAsString()).\nTSRM: make CG, EG, SCNG and AG compile-time offsets.\nDeprecate returning values from __construct() and __destruct().\nbase_convert, bindex, hexdec and octdec now raise a notice when they cannot precisely convert the given number.\nAdded error_include_args INI option to make the display of function arguments consistent in error output.\nFixed GHSA-8mjj-2r7p-4hg2 (Use-after-free in magic method backtraces can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-129474)\nFixed GHSA-2fjv-p558-g82m (Use-after-free via repopulation of last_fatal_error_backtrace global after shutdown). (CVE-2026-129182)\nAdded NUL-byte validation to BCMath functions.\nPassing an object for the Bzip2 {de}compression stream filter is now deprecated. Use get_object_vars() on the object instead.\nReject oversized input in bzdecompress().\nFixed *tojd() functions and cal_to_jd() truncating arguments outside the int range instead of rejecting them.\nFixed GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during PATH_INFO correction). (CVE-2026-129538)\nFixed bug GH-24697 (PHP_HTTP_PARSER_STRICT build option doesn't work).\nFixed bug GH-9670 (List -C and -q in the CLI help).\nFixed bug GH-23242 (PHP development server does not support Expect 100-continue flow control).\nFixed bug GH-25008 (com_event_sink() and com_print_typeinfo() crash resolving an event source with no loaded typelib).\nFix use-after-free of CURLOPT_STDERR stream on cloned curl handle.\nFix UAF on clone due to callback data pointer mismatch.\nSet content length using CURLOPT_POSTFIELDSIZE_LARGE instead of CURLOPT_POSTFIELDSIZE. This makes it possible to post strings larger than 2GB on some platforms, e.g. Windows.\nImproved cURL option validation errors to include the option name.\nRaise a value error when the callback registered with CURLOPT_READFUNCTION returns an unexpected long.\nFix bug GH-16513 (curl: exceptions in callbacks do not abort the request).\nAdded CURLOPT_SEEKFUNCTION and the CURL_SEEKFUNC_OK, CURL_SEEKFUNC_FAIL and CURL_SEEKFUNC_CANTSEEK constants, letting libcurl rewind a streamed request body to resend it on a redirect, multi-pass authentication or a retried reused connection.\nAdd support for CURLINFO_SIZE_DELIVERED (libcurl >= 8.20.0).\nUpdate timelib to 2026.03 (Derick)\nFixed bug GH-20503 (Assertion failure with ext/date DateInterval property hash construction).\nFixed bug GH-24350 (MINIT reads a stale external tz database after an in-process module restart).\nFixed bug GH-11368 (idate() doesn't work for the year -1).\nFixed GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv (Timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-129496)\nFixed bug GH-24641 (ndbm backend never checks dbm_open() return value, NULL deref on first use after a failed open).\nFixed a use-after-free when reflected attribute setters replace an attribute whose child still has a live wrapper.\nFix error paths in dom_xml_serializing_a_document_node().\nFixed reference cycles through DOMXPath and XSLTProcessor php:function callback arguments and return values not being collectable.\nFixed a typo in the DOMException message for INUSE_ATTRIBUTE_ERR.\nFixed bug GH-22624 (use-after-free via DOMNameSpaceNode after DOMDocument::xinclude()).\nFixed Dom\\DtdNamedNodeMap integer dimension access so negative indexes return NULL and indexes outside the int range throw ValueError instead of returning the first entity or notation.\nFixed bug GH-22623 (use after free with namespace nodes from XSLTProcessor::registerFunctions())/ (David Carlier)\nFixed bug GH-22554 (use-after-free with XPath callback returning a node from a foreign document).\nRemoved LIBXML_XINCLUDE from valid options for XMLDocument, as it was a no-op.\nReadonly DOM properties are now declared with asymmetric visibility (public private(set)). ReflectionProperty::isWritable() reports them correctly, and external writes raise \"Cannot modify private(set) property\" instead of the previous readonly modification error.\nFixed Dom\\Notation nodes missing tree connection, so that ownerDocument, parentNode, isConnected and baseURI now return correct values, and textContent returns NULL per the DOM specification.\nFixed GHSA-x8r7-mg3g-74hg (Double free during DOM XML serialization). (CVE-2026-129501)\nMade php-cli functionality available in embed builds.\nAdded support for reading EXIF metadata from WebP images (GH-19904).\nFixed bug GH-24582 (Memory leaks in ext/ffi parser when finalize_type() bails out).\nFixed bug GH-24289 (finfo::file() reports the wrong argument number for an invalid $filename).\nFixed bug GH-20679 (finfo_file() doesn't work on remote resources).\nFixed bug #66095 (Hide libmagic dynamic symbols).\nFixed crash and stack memory disclosure in the worker output logging with a pool name longer than the message prefix buffer or log_limit.\nFixed GHSA-jm4m-qfqx-967m (PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local privilege escalation). (CVE-2026-129291)\nFixed memory leaks of the _GET string on the status page error and HEAD request paths.\nFixed use-after-free of the scoreboard copy when logging invalid status values.\nFixed null pointer dereference in fpm_get_status() when the scoreboard copy fails.\nFixed bug GH-24229 (fcgi_close() passes shutdown() a literal 1, which is SHUT_RD in WASI).\nFixed GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP request body). (CVE-2026-129289)\nFixed GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user and script fields). (CVE-2026-129292)\nFix double free in ext/ftp data_accept() on accept failure.\nFixed imageaffinematrixget() to enforce the documented array|float type for the $options parameter.\nimagesetstyle()/imagefilter()/imagecrop() check array argument entries types.\nAdded optional $definitely_prime output parameter to gmp_prevprime().\nFixed GMP power and shift operators to reject GMP right operands outside the unsigned long range instead of silently truncating them.\nFixed GMP integer string parsing to reject strings containing NUL bytes instead of silently truncating them.\nFixed GMP error messages that referenced outdated parameter names.\nFixed bug GH-22549 (Assertion failure / UB on a compound GMP power or shift assignment with a negative exponent).\ngmp_fact() reject values larger than unsigned long.\ngmp_pow/binomial/root/rootrem and shift/pow operators reject values larger than unsigned long.\nGMP exponentiation and shift operators now emit a deprecation warning when converting a float right operand to int loses precision.\nFix GOST and Snefru digests of 512 MiB or more.\nFixed hash_file() reporting argument #1 ($algo) instead of argument #2 ($filename) when the filename contains null bytes.\nFixed IntlDateFormatter parse functions truncating an $offset below INT_MIN.\nFixed Collator::sortWithSortKeys() allocating fixed 2MiB buffers regardless of array size.\nFixed Spoofchecker methods not recording the ICU error code when an ICU call fails.\nFixed idn_to_ascii() and idn_to_utf8() reporting argument #2 ($flags) instead of argument #3 ($variant) for an invalid IDNA variant, and the domain length error message printing a literal \"d\" instead of the limit.\nAdded static methods IntlDatePatternGenerator::getSkeleton() and IntlDatePatternGenerator::getBaseSkeleton().\nFixed Collator::sort(), collator_sort(), Collator::asort(), and collator_asort() to report UTF-8/UTF-16 conversion errors through the intl error handler instead of emitting a warning and continuing with an empty string.\nImplemented GH-20255 (Add a predefined calendar constant in IntlDateFormatter for the proleptic gregorian calendar).\nFixed grammatical issues in Normalizer invalid form and IntlCalendar time zone offset error messages.\nRemoved the dependency on the ICU IO library.\nFixed NumberFormatter::parse() and NumberFormatter::parseCurrency() to reject offset values outside the 32-bit range instead of silently truncating them.\nIntlDateFormatter::parse()/datefmt_parse() and IntlDateFormatter::localtime()/datefmt_localtime() now raise TypeError when the offset argument is not of type int.\nFixed malformed ResourceBundle::get() error message when fallback is disabled.\nAdded Locale::getDisplayKeyword() and Locale::getDisplayKeywordValue(), with the alias of locale_get_display_keyword() and locale_get_display_keyword_value() respectively.\nAdded IntlNumberRangeFormatter class to format an interval of two numbers with a given skeleton, locale, collapse type and identity fallback.\nPassing a non-stringable object as a time zone to Intl time zone argument handling now raises TypeError instead of Error.\nIntlBreakIterator::getLocale() now raises ValueError for invalid locale types.\nFixed MessageFormatter::parse() and parseMessage() returning PHP_INT_MIN as float rather than int on 64-bit platforms.\nFixed UConverter::transcode() silently truncating from_subst and to_subst option lengths greater than 127 bytes.\nFixed IntlIterator::current() to return NULL instead of an undefined value when the iterator is not positioned on a valid element.\nFixed json_encode() leaving the recursion guard set on objects with hooked properties after running out of memory while escaping a property name.\nFixed json_encode() silently narrowing $depth values outside the int range, which wrapped to an unrelated depth.\nFixed json_encode() continuing to encode after an array or object key failed to encode.\nReport unterminated JSON strings as syntax errors.\nImprove performance error position tracking during JSON decoding.\nEnriched JSON last error / exception message with error location.\nFix crash in ldap_exop_sync() when $response_data is omitted.\nFixed negative mbstring.regex_stack_limit and mbstring.regex_retry_limit on 32bit platforms.\nFixed bug GH-23958 (truncated encoding names resolving to full names).\nFixed out-of-bounds read in php_mb_rfc1867_getword() on a multibyte lead byte at the end of a multipart field name.\nUpdated Unicode data tables to Unicode 18.0 (Yuya Hamada)\nPassing objects to mb_convert_variables() is now deprecated.\nini_set() with mbstring.detect_order changes the order of mb_detect_order as intended, since mbstring.detect_order is an INI_ALL setting.\nAdded GB18030-2022 to default encoding list for zh-CN.\nThe mysqli_get_charset() function and mysqli::get_charset() method are now deprecated.\nThe mysqli_stmt_init() function and mysqli::stmt_init() method are now deprecated.\nInstantiation of mysqli_stmt without providing the $query parameter is now deprecated.\nFixed bug GH-24609 (OK packets without an info message rejected on x32 builds).\nFixed bug GH-24293 (Segfault on connect with an empty password to a MariaDB PAM account).\nFixed bug GH-25036 (odbc_prepare() corrupts the heap when the driver cannot describe a parameter).\nodbc_error() and odbc_errormsg() now also report SQLColAttribute failures.\nFixed bug GH-24397 (Assertion failure when dumping JIT IR).\nFixed tracing JIT returning a wrapped integer instead of a float on integer overflow after an integer was compared with a float or numeric-string literal.\nFixed use-after-free in JIT ASSIGN_DIM_OP when concatenating into an empty array element.\nFixed bug GH-24396 (Assertion failure in zend_jit_def_reg() \"reg forwarding\" with chained Pi nodes).\nFixed JIT treating an array as packed after a string key write turned it into a hash.\nFixed bug GH-24436 (Tracing JIT: keep the SEND_VAL type guard after assigning to a reference).\nFixed bug GH-24745 (File cache loses attributes on constants on 32-bit builds).\nFixed bug GH-17733 (System entropy does not take into account function order, resulting in wrong functions possibly called in different configurations).\nFixed bug GH-24438 (Preserve indirect types in JIT side traces).\nFixed bug GH-24577 (CE-cache flag on interned class name visible before map_ptr offset).\nFixed tracing JIT losing register-allocated CVs when an interrupt is handled at the end of a loop trace.\nFixed bug GH-24675 (function with >~1.7 MB of machine code corrupts JIT buffer accounting).\nFixed JIT segfault on switch over a string reference holding a non-string value.\nFixed AArch64 JIT encoding of invalid logical immediates.\nFixed JIT crashes when handling a VM interrupt with a stale saved opline in the tailcall VM.\nFixed function JIT misinterpreting VM-enter results after an interrupt callback in the CALL and TAILCALL VMs.\nFixed unsound shift_left_overflows range when shift wraps.\nFixed bug GH-23572 (Tracing JIT calls the wrong method for self::/parent:: static calls in trait methods shared by several classes).\nFix block pass dropping ZEND_FAST_CALL OP2 definition.\nFixed bug GH-23626 (orphaned temporaries cause leaks and assertions).\nFix preloaded functions JIT-compiled on load being overwritten after restart.\nFix opcache.interned_strings_buffer being 0 in threads started later (ZTS).\nFixed potential infinite recursion/hang (HYBRID/TAILCALL respectively) when zend_interrupt_function resets EG(vm_interrupt).\nFix JIT losing the called scope of self::/parent:: calls in included files.\nFixed preloaded functions not JIT-compiled again after OPcache restart.\nFixed bug GH-24988 (Incorrect opcode range check causes bugs with exceptions in function JIT).\nFixed bug GH-17626 (JIT corrupts an opline handler when blacklisting a root trace at the opcache.jit_max_root_traces limit, causing spurious \"Too few arguments\" errors and crashes).\nFix type inference of ADD_ARRAY_UNPACK with integer keys.\nFix too wide type inference for ASSIGN_DIM_OP.\nFix OSS-Fuzz #568005340 (FETCH_DIM_FUNC_ARG partial conversion).\nFix exception checks due to NAN warnings and object empty()'s.\nFixed bug GH-24270 (JIT loses the called scope of self:: and parent:: calls in closures).\nFixed bug GH-24337 (JIT: segfault when decrementing a non-numeric string property).\nFixed bug GH-24185 (Windows ZTS: random access violations with OPcache JIT in multi-process setups).\nFix SIGFPE on LONG_MIN % -1 with a constant divisor.\nFixed bug GH-24388 (Tracing JIT: segfault when a trace runs out of side exits).\nFixed bug GH-24391 (JIT switch on constant null takes default instead of case 0).\nFixed bug GH-24206 (Tracing JIT loses loop-carried CV when its loop PHI is reloaded from memory).\nFixed bug GH-24386 (JIT: register operand must be loaded before the typed reference check).\nFixed bug GH-24437 (JIT: Fix OP_DATA read from an unwritten slot in zend_jit_assign_dim_op()).\nFixed bug GH-24398 (JIT: minimal JIT segfault when a hooked property is passed to a run-time-resolved function).\nFixed bug GH-24389 (Tracing JIT: type guard on entry of an inlined call exits with an uninitialized opline).\nRe-enable JIT for ZTS builds on Apple Silicon.\nFixed bug GH-20051 (apache2 shutdowns when restart is requested during preloading).\nFixed build with OpenSSL 4.1.\nFixed bug GH-24784 (openssl_pkcs7_read() and openssl_cms_read() overwrite certificates with CRLs).\nAdded $salt_length parameter to openssl_sign() and openssl_verify() with new OPENSSL_RSA_PSS_SALTLEN_* constants.\nImplemented GH-20310 (No critical extension indication in openssl_x509_parse() output).\nAdded TLS session resumption support for streams with new context options and Openssl\\Session class.\nAdded TLS external PSK support for streams with new context options and Openssl\\Psk class.\nAdded TLS 1.3 early data (0-RTT) support for streams with new context options early_data, max_early_data and early_data_cb.\nAdded stream crypto status for exposing OpenSSL WANT_READ / WANT_WRITE.\nFixed the declared signature of pcntl_signal(), whose $restart_syscalls argument accepts null and defaults to it.\npcntl_exec() now throws a ValueError if the $args array is not a list array.\nFixed invalid ATTR_ORACLE_NULLS values being accepted and truncated.\nFixed a duplicate warning when ATTR_STATEMENT_CLASS is rejected on a persistent connection.\nFixed constructor option errors naming argument #3 ($password) instead of argument #4 ($options).\nFixed pdo_raise_impl_error() emitting a warning under ERRMODE_SILENT.\nFixed bug GH-25006 (getColumnMeta() reads out of bounds for an out-of-range column index).\nFixed bug GH-24461 (DISCARD ALL on persistent connection cleanup drops PgBouncer's prepared statements).\nFixed a use-after-free when a persistent connection receives a notice after the request that called Pdo\\Pgsql::setNoticeCallback() has ended.\nFixed crash when a persistent connection fails.\nAdded Pdo\\Pgsql::ATTR_CHUNK_SIZE to fetch a result set in chunks of the given number of rows.\nClear session-local state disconnect-equivalent processing.\nFixed bug GH-24990 (Statement unusable after a failed execute()).\nFixed the pg_insert(), pg_update() and pg_delete() flag error messages, which did not name the set of flags actually accepted.\nFixed the class name casing of pg_close_stmt()'s connection parameter.\nEnabled 64 bits support for pg_lo_truncate()/pg_lo_tell() if the server supports it.\npg_fetch_object() now surfaces non-instantiable class errors before fetching, resolves the constructor via the get_constructor handler, and reports the empty-constructor ValueError on the $constructor_args argument.\nFixed bug GH-25093 (Phar::webPhar() redirect reads past the request URI).\nFixed bug GH-25089 (Heap buffer over-read via crafted alias size in zip-based phar).\nFixed bug GH-8469 (Phar::decompressFiles() and Phar::compressFiles() retain compressed contents after changing compression).\nFixed bug GH-24740 (Oversized tar metadata exhausts the memory limit).\nFixed bug GH-25090 (UAF in phar rename() of an entry with metadata).\nFixed bug GH-25091 (UAF in phar rename() when source and destination are equal).\nFixed bug GH-25092 (Double free in Phar::copy() on link and mounted entries).\nFixed bug GH-24531 (Crash when modifying a zip-based phar whose file was renamed).\nFixed Phar::buildFromIterator() accepting a negative getMTime() on 32bit platforms.\nFixed Phar archives being automatically detected when \".phar\" only occurs in a directory name or is not a filename extension in an included file's path.\nFixed grammatical issues and outdated terminology in Phar error messages.\nSupport reference values in Phar::mungServer().\nInvalid values now throw in Phar::mungServer() instead of being silently ignored.\nFixed a bypass of the magic \".phar\" directory protection in Phar::addEmptyDir() for paths starting with \"/.phar\".\nPhar::addEmptyDir() now allows non-magic directory names that merely share the \".phar\" prefix.\nSupport overridden methods in SplFileInfo for getMTime() and getPathname() when building a phar.\nMark Phar::buildFromIterator() base directory argument as a path.\nFixed GHSA-68fq-fh7h-f8gr (PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade). (CVE-2026-128090)\nFixed GH-22480 (Use-after-free when re-watching an already-watched variable).\nFixed posix_setrlimit() rejecting POSIX_RLIMIT_INFINITY on Solaris.\nFixed a crash in readline_info() when completion_append_character contains a non-ASCII byte.\nFixed class constant completion in the interactive shell.\nAdded ReflectionAttribute::inNamespace(), ReflectionAttribute::getNamespaceName(), and ReflectionAttribute::getShortName().\nFixed bug GH-21362 (ReflectionMethod::invoke/invokeArgs() did not verify Closure instance identity for Closure::__invoke()).\nFixed infinite loop in sapi_header_op() for headers of 4 GiB or more.\nValidate whole session ID instead of stopping at the first NUL byte.\nFixed session_write_close() keeping the save handler open when the session data cannot be encoded.\nFixed bug GH-23056 (missing handler name in session write warning).\nSessionHandler::validateId() is now implemented, so session.use_strict_mode applies to the built-in handler.\nIt is now deprecated to pass an object that does not implement the create_sid() and validateId() methods.\nA deprecation is now emitted when implementing SessionHandlerInterface on a class which doesn't define the create_sid() or validateId() methods, as those will be moved from SessionUpdateTimestampHandlerInterface and SessionIdInterface to SessionHandlerInterface.\nFixed bug 71162 (updateTimestamp never called when session data is empty).\nNull bytes in session.cookie_path, session.cookie_domain, and session.cache_limiter are now rejected with a warning.\nsession.cookie_samesite now rejects invalid values with a warning; only \"Strict\", \"Lax\", \"None\", or \"\" are accepted.\nsession.cookie_lifetime now rejects non-integer and out-of-range values with a warning.\nSession file GC now recursively cleans nested subdirectories when session.save_path uses the dirdepth prefix.\nChanged defaults of session.use_strict_mode (now 1), session.cookie_httponly (now 1) and session.cookie_samesite (now \"Lax\").\nFixed GHSA-fm2m-fjf5-v3cp (Partially overwritten session files can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-126714)\nFixed GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx (Session serializer mismatch can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-115560)\nFixed GHSA-g3vh-838c-65v7 (Use-after-free after interrupted session shutdown). (CVE-2026-129481)\nFixed bug GH-9945 (shmop_open() silently truncates keys outside the key_t range).\nSimpleXMLElement::__construct() now raises a ValueError when the $data argument contains NUL bytes.\nIt is now possible to use the AES192, AES192C, AES256, and AES256C as SNMPv3 security protocols if the underlying library supports them.\nIt is now possible to reset the MIB tree using the new snmp_init_mib() function.\nAdditional MIB parsing and output control functionality has been exposed via the snmp_set_mib_option(), snmp_set_output_option(), snmp_set_string_output_format() functions, the $numeric_index, $numeric_timeticks, $extended_index, $dont_print_units, $escape_quotes, $print_hex_text SNMP properties, and the SNMP::setOidOutputFormat(), SNMP::setStringOutputFormat() methods.\nFixed bug GH-23686 (SoapClient only strips `Authorization: Basic` when a WSDL imports from another host).\nFixed header injection through the Content-Type context option, the soapaction and the cookie names and values.\nFixed the SoapClient and SoapServer \"classmap\" option to reject arrays containing integer keys, and made SoapClient throw TypeError/ValueError for invalid \"classmap\" options.\nFixed bug GH-22585 (OOM on bailout with uninitialized do_request() parameters).\nFixed xsd:hexBinary decoding to reject odd-length values instead of silently truncating the last nibble.\nMade SOAP encoding errors report the affected type or failing operation instead of the generic \"Violation of encoding rules\" message.\nSoap::__setCookie() when cookie name is a digit is now not stored and represented as a string anymore but a int.\nFixed bug GH-21421 (SoapClient typemap property breaks engine assumptions).\nWSDL/XML Schema parsing now rejects out-of-range integer values for occurrence constraints and integer restriction facets. Negative minOccurs and maxOccurs values are rejected as well.\nFixed GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg (SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions). (CVE-2026-15353)\nFixed GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 (SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references). (CVE-2026-129506)\nFixed bug GH-24748 (socket_set_option() crashes with declared object properties).\nFixed socket_set_option() with SO_ATTACH_REUSEPORT_CBPF and a zero value, which detached the classic BPF filter instead of the reuseport program.\nFixed socket_set_option() validation error messages for UDP_SEGMENT and TCP_USER_TIMEOUT, and SO_LINGER options.\nAdded the TCP_USER_TIMEOUT constant for Linux to set the maximum time in milliseconds transmitted data can remain unacknowledged.\nAdded AF_UNSPEC support for sock_addrinfo_lookup() as a sole umbrella for AF_INET* family only.\nFixed GH-20532 (socket_addrinfo_lookup gives the error code with a new optional parameter).\nAdded AF_PACKET support completion for socket_sendto()/socket_recvfrom().\nAdded support for the libsodium 1.0.22 KEM APIs (X-Wing and ML-KEM768).\nFixed incorrect parameter name in sodium_add(), sodium_memcmp(), and sodium_compare() length-mismatch error messages.\nAdded support for libsodium 1.0.21 IPcrypt and XOF APIs.\npwhash argument-validation errors now throw ValueError instead of SodiumException.\nFixed bug GH-24264 (Unwind/GracefulExit discarded in spl_iterators.c).\nFixed bug GH-23385 (SplDoublyLinkedList::serialize() use-after-free when __serialize() removes an element).\nThe following SplFileObject methods have been deprecated SplFileObject::fgetcsv(), SplFileObject::fputcsv(), SplFileObject::setCsvControl(), and SplFileObject::getCsvControl().\nThe spl_classes() function is now deprecated, use ReflectionExtension::getClassNames() instead.\nThe spl_object_hash() function is now deprecated, use spl_object_id() instead.\nThe following ArrayIterator methods are now deprecated: * ArrayIterator::getFlags() * ArrayIterator::setFlags() * ArrayIterator::asort() * ArrayIterator::ksort() * ArrayIterator::uasort() * ArrayIterator::uksort() * ArrayIterator::natsort() * ArrayIterator::natcasesort() * ArrayIterator::unserialize() * ArrayIterator::serialize() (Girgias)\nDirectoryIterator key can now work better with filesystem supporting larger directory indexing.\nFixed bug GH-21831 (SplObjectStorage::removeAllExcept() use-after-free with re-entrant getHash()).\nFix bugs GH-8561, GH-8562, GH-8563, and GH-8564 (Fixing various SplFileObject iterator desync bugs).\nFix bug GH-22062 (SplDoublyLinkedList iterator UAF via destructor releasing next node).\nFix NUL byte truncation in sqlite3 TEXT column handling.\nFixed memory leaks in checkdnsrr() and dns_check_record() on Windows.\nFixed __unserialize() and __wakeup() being called for objects with a missing closing brace.\nFixed bug GH-24308 (Request shutdown calls closelog() even when syslog was not opened by PHP).\nFixed bug GH-24552 (Case-insensitive substr_compare(), ksort() and krsort() are still locale-dependent).\nFix use-after-free in Randomizer::shuffleArray() when the engine throws.\nFixed password_get_info() and password_needs_rehash() accepting malformed bcrypt costs.\nFixed proc_open() null descriptor not being inheritable on Windows.\nDon't share the unserialize() context with enum autoloaders.\nFixed bug GH-24399 (usleep() and time_nanosleep() ignore queued APCs on Windows).\nFixed glob() not negating bracket expressions that start with \"^\".\nFixed bug GH-24605 (var_export() crashes on deeply nested arrays and objects).\nFixed bug #60110 (fclose(), file_put_contents(), copy() do not return false properly).\nFixed bug GH-23780 (unserialize('') fails silently).\nFixed an out-of-bounds read when following a redirect response with an empty Location header.\nFixed incorrect parameter name in convert_uudecode() warning.\nAdded support for the \"<\" and \">\" endianness modifiers in pack() and unpack() format codes.\nPassing an object as the $data argument to http_build_query() is now deprecated. The interpretation of object values within $data as arrays is also deprecated. Convert objects to arrays with get_object_vars() before calling the function.\nAdded the \"filter.max_filter_count\" stream context option for php://filter URLs. Using more than 16 filters without configuring this option is now deprecated.\nThe metaphone() function is now deprecated, use a userland phonetic matching library instead.\nFixed bug GH-23006 (phpcredits() full-page HTML title says phpinfo()).\nThe following functions now raise a ValueError when the $filename argument contains NUL bytes: fileperms(), fileinode(), filesize(), fileowner(), filegroup(), fileatime(), filemtime(), filectime(), filetype(), is_writable(), is_readable(), is_executable(), is_file(), is_dir(), is_link(), file_exists(), lstat(), stat().\nFixed bug GH-22818 (stream_filter_register() orphaned user_filter_map on shutdown re-registration).\nPassing an object to array_walk{_recursive} is now deprecated. Use get_object_vars() on the object instead.\nThe is_double() function is now deprecated, use is_float() instead.\nThe is_long() and is_integer() functions are now deprecated, use is_int() instead.\nThe doubleval() function is now deprecated, use floatval() instead.\nThe strcoll() function is now deprecated, use Collator::compare() instead.\nThe SORT_LOCALE_STRING constant for the family of sort functions is now deprecated, use one of the following functions instead: * Collator::asort() * Collator::sort() * Collator::sortWithSortKeys() (Girgias)\nFixed setlocale() to reject locale names containing NUL bytes instead of silently truncating them, and to reject arrays passed after the $locales argument or additional arguments passed after an array $locales argument.\nFixed sleep() and usleep() to reject values that overflow the underlying unsigned int timeout.\nFixed bug GH-22671 (assert.bail aborts the process when the assert callback throws an exception whose reporting re-throws).\nAdded form feed (\\f) in the default trimmed characters of trim(), rtrim() and ltrim().\nInvalid mode values now throw in array_filter() instead of being silently defaulted to 0.\nFixed bug GH-21058 (error_log() crashes with message_type 3 and null destination).\nFixed bug GH-13204 (glob() fails if square bracket is in current directory).\nAdd array size maximum to array_diff().\npathinfo() raises a ValueError with an invalid $flags argument.\nPassing an invalid flag value to the second argument of scandir() will now throw a ValueError.\narray_change_key_case() now raises a ValueError when an invalid $case argument value is passed.\nlinkinfo() now raises a ValueError when the argument is an empty string.\ngetenv() and putenv() now raises a ValueError when the first argument contains NUL bytes.\ndl() now raises a ValueError when the $extension_filename argument contains NUL bytes.\nopenlog() now raises a ValueError when the $prefix argument contains NUL bytes.\nparse_str() now raises a ValueError when the $string argument contains NUL bytes.\nproc_open() now raises a ValueError when the $cwd argument contains NUL bytes.\nini_get_all() now includes the built-in default value in the details.\nFixed bug GH-17384 (number_format() may exhaust memory with decimals outside the range from -2147483648 to 2147483647).\nFixed bug GH-20862 (null pointer dereference in php_mail_detect_multiple_crlf via error_log).\nFixed GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j (Mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext). (CVE-2026-128064)\nFixed GHSA-mmf9-xm3v-hg2x (Denial of service through folded HTTP response headers). (CVE-2026-127960)\nFixed bug GH-24508 (HTTP wrapper leaks the dechunk filter when header parsing fails after Transfer-Encoding).\nFixed bug GH-24509 (HTTP wrapper leaks Location buffer on empty Location header).\nFix out-of-bounds reads parsing ftp:// wrapper server replies.\nAdded so_rcvbuf and so_sndbuf stream socket context options, setting the socket receive and send buffer sizes in bytes.\nAdded a new IO copy API used by php_stream_copy_to_stream_ex() that leverages platform primitives (sendfile, splice, copy_file_range, TransmitFile) for faster stream copying.\nAdded new stream errors API including new StreamException, StreamError classes, StreamErrorStore, StreamErrorMode, StreamErrorCode enums, stream_last_errors() and stream_clear_errors() functions, error_mode, error_store and error_handler stream context options and extending some stream functions with context param.\nAdded so_keepalive, tcp_keepidle, tcp_keepintvl and tcp_keepcnt stream socket context options.\nAdded so_reuseaddr streams context socket option that allows disabling address resuse.\nAdded so_linger stream socket context option.\nAllowed filtered streams to be casted as fd for select.\nFixed bug GH-21221 (Prevent closing of innerstream of php://temp stream).\nImproved stream_socket_server() bind failure error reporting.\nFixed bug #49874 (ftell() and fseek() inconsistency when using stream filters).\nFixed shm_attach() to throw ValueError for keys outside the key_t range.\nFixed tidy_repair_string(), tidy_repair_file(), tidy::repairString() and tidy::repairFile() rejecting null for $encoding.\nUpgrade to uriparser 1.0.3. (CVE-2026-48841)\nFixed GHSA-mg3p-mxj9-g2mm (Incorrect RFC 3986 URI serialization for oversized input). (CVE-2026-129438)\nFixed bug GH-25009 (GetConsoleTitleW() buffer size passed in bytes).\nFixed sapi_windows_cp_set() and sapi_windows_cp_conv() accepting a negative codepage on 32bit platforms.\nReject broken libzip versions 1.3.1, 1.7.0 and 1.12.0 during Windows configuration.\nExcluded libzip 1.12.0 due to a regression preventing additions and replacements in torrentzip archives.\nFixed use-after-free when re-entering ZipArchive during destruction or a close warning, and rejected opening streams while closing.\nFixed a use-after-free when a ZipArchive method that modifies the archive is called from a progress or cancel callback during close().\nFixed bug GH-23899 (Assertion failure when a cancel callback returns an invalid type during shutdown).\nFixed bug GH-22176 (memory leak with ZipArchive::registerCancelBack() is used with reference returning function during shutdown).\nZipArchive::addGlob() and ZipArchive::addPattern() now raise a TypeError for invalid \"remove_all_path\", \"comp_method\", \"comp_flags\", and \"enc_method\" options instead of emitting a warning.\nFixed bug GH-21682 (ZipArchive instances should not be serializable). serialize()/unserialize() now throw unless a subclass overrides __serialize()/__unserialize().\nFixed ZipArchive callback being called after executor has shut down.\nSupport minimum version for libzip dependency updated to 1.0.0.\nFixed bug GH-24533 (zlib.lib could not be found because zlib 1.3.2 CMake build does not emit it).\nFixed use-after-free when an error handler removes a failing zlib.inflate filter (GH-24176).\nFixed bug GH-22142 (Assertion failure in deflate_init() when an option object has uninitialised typed properties).\nPassing an object for the zlib deflate and inflate stream filter is now deprecated. Use get_object_vars() on the object instead.\nPassing an object to the $option argument to deflate_init and inflate_init is now deprecated. Use get_object_vars() on the object instead.\ndeflate_init() now raises a TypeError when the value for option \"level\", \"memory\", \"window\", or \"strategy\" is not of type int.\ninflate_init() now raises a TypeError when the value for option \"window\" is not of type int.\nFixed bug GH-24184 (System ID not being reinitialized after an Apache graceful restart, potentially causing incompatible OPcache file cache entries to be reused).\nFixed memory leak when an exception already contains the pending exception in its previous chain.\nFixed bug GH-23979 (Nullsafe operator must not flush delayed oplines of an enclosing function).\nFixed memory manager keeping a block reallocated to exactly the size of the next smaller bin in its larger bin, which efree_size() then freed into the wrong one.\nFixed bug GH-24081 (User opcode handlers resume execution against a stale frame under ZEND_VM_KIND_TAILCALL).\nFixed bug GH-24218 (Invalid opcode for count() of a literal array without SCCP).\nFix throwing behaviour with recursive arrays in VM.\nFixed skipped catch block when switching fibers during exception unwinding (Nicolas Grekas)\nFix escape analysis for objects implementing ArrayAccess.\nFix UAF for resolved callable zval.\nFix memory leak for nested HTTP calls.\nFix function and constant imports in compile_to_ast and add support for grouping.\nFixed bug GH-24668 (zend_set_local_var() leaks the previous value of an existing CV).\nFixed unmapping of an unrelated range when the aligned chunk mmap fails (Marti2203).\nFixed AST printing dropping final on class constants and properties, and abstract on properties.\nFixed AST export of readonly anonymous classes dropping the readonly modifier.\nFixed memory leak of a duplicate named argument in new in initializer.\nFixed bug GH-25061 ($x = $x - 1 on null is optimized to PRE_DEC).\nFixed first-class callables to static methods in trait constant expressions resolving to the method of the first using class and bypassing visibility checks.\nFixed GHSA-8mjj-2r7p-4hg2 (Use-after-free in magic method backtraces can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-129474)\nFixed GHSA-2fjv-p558-g82m (Use-after-free via repopulation of last_fatal_error_backtrace global after shutdown). (CVE-2026-129182)\nFixed GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during PATH_INFO correction). (CVE-2026-129538)\nFixed bug GH-24697 (PHP_HTTP_PARSER_STRICT build option doesn't work).\nFixed bug GH-9670 (List -C and -q in the CLI help).\nFixed bug GH-25008 (com_event_sink() and com_print_typeinfo() crash resolving an event source with no loaded typelib).\nFix use-after-free of CURLOPT_STDERR stream on cloned curl handle.\nFix UAF on clone due to callback data pointer mismatch.\nFixed bug GH-20503 (Assertion failure with ext/date DateInterval property hash construction).\nFixed bug GH-24350 (MINIT reads a stale external tz database after an in-process module restart).\nFixed GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv (Timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-129496)\nFixed bug GH-24641 (ndbm backend never checks dbm_open() return value, NULL deref on first use after a failed open).\nFixed a use-after-free when reflected attribute setters replace an attribute whose child still has a live wrapper.\nFix error paths in dom_xml_serializing_a_document_node().\nFixed bug GH-25118 (Dom\\HTMLDocument::createFromString() crash on OOM).\nFixed GHSA-x8r7-mg3g-74hg (Double free during DOM XML serialization). (CVE-2026-129501)\nFixed bug GH-24582 (Memory leaks in ext/ffi parser when finalize_type() bails out).\nFixed bug GH-24289 (finfo::file() reports the wrong argument number for an invalid $filename).\nFixed bug GH-24229 (fcgi_close() passes shutdown() a literal 1, which is SHUT_RD in WASI).\nFixed crash and stack memory disclosure in the worker output logging with a pool name longer than the message prefix buffer or log_limit.\nFixed GHSA-jm4m-qfqx-967m (PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local privilege escalation). (CVE-2026-129291)\nFixed memory leaks of the _GET string on the status page error and HEAD request paths.\nFixed use-after-free of the scoreboard copy when logging invalid status values.\nFixed null pointer dereference in fpm_get_status() when the scoreboard copy fails.\nFixed GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP request body). (CVE-2026-129289)\nFixed GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user and script fields). (CVE-2026-129292)\nFix double free in ext/ftp data_accept() on accept failure.\nFix GOST and Snefru digests of 512 MiB or more.\nFixed IntlDateFormatter parse functions truncating an $offset below INT_MIN.\nFixed json_encode() leaving the recursion guard set on objects with hooked properties after running out of memory while escaping a property name.\nFixed json_encode() silently narrowing $depth values outside the int range, which wrapped to an unrelated depth.\nFixed json_encode() continuing to encode after an array or object key failed to encode.\nFix crash in ldap_exop_sync() when $response_data is omitted.\nFixed bug GH-23958 (truncated encoding names resolving to full names).\nFixed out-of-bounds read in php_mb_rfc1867_getword() on a multibyte lead byte at the end of a multipart field name.\nFixed negative mbstring.regex_stack_limit and mbstring.regex_retry_limit on 32bit platforms.\nFixed bug GH-24293 (Segfault on connect with an empty password to a MariaDB PAM account).\nFixed bug GH-24609 (OK packets without an info message rejected on x32 builds).\nFixed bug GH-25036 (odbc_prepare() corrupts the heap when the driver cannot describe a parameter).\nFixed bug GH-24397 (Assertion failure when dumping JIT IR).\nFixed tracing JIT returning a wrapped integer instead of a float on integer overflow after an integer was compared with a float or numeric-string literal.\nFixed bug GH-17626 (JIT corrupts an opline handler when blacklisting a root trace at the opcache.jit_max_root_traces limit, causing spurious \"Too few arguments\" errors and crashes).\nFix type inference of ADD_ARRAY_UNPACK with integer keys.\nFix too wide type inference for ASSIGN_DIM_OP.\nFix OSS-Fuzz #568005340 (FETCH_DIM_FUNC_ARG partial conversion).\nFix exception checks due to NAN warnings and object empty()'s.\nFixed bug GH-24270 (JIT loses the called scope of self:: and parent:: calls in closures).\nFixed bug GH-24337 (JIT: segfault when decrementing a non-numeric string property).\nFixed bug GH-24185 (Windows ZTS: random access violations with OPcache JIT in multi-process setups).\nFix SIGFPE on LONG_MIN % -1 with a constant divisor.\nFixed bug GH-24388 (Tracing JIT: segfault when a trace runs out of side exits).\nFixed bug GH-24391 (JIT switch on constant null takes default instead of case 0).\nFixed bug GH-24206 (Tracing JIT loses loop-carried CV when its loop PHI is reloaded from memory).\nFixed bug GH-24386 (JIT: register operand must be loaded before the typed reference check).\nFixed bug GH-24437 (JIT: Fix OP_DATA read from an unwritten slot in zend_jit_assign_dim_op()).\nFixed bug GH-24398 (JIT: minimal JIT segfault when a hooked property is passed to a run-time-resolved function).\nFixed bug GH-24389 (Tracing JIT: type guard on entry of an inlined call exits with an uninitialized opline).\nFixed use-after-free in JIT ASSIGN_DIM_OP when concatenating into an empty array element.\nFixed bug GH-24396 (Assertion failure in zend_jit_def_reg() \"reg forwarding\" with chained Pi nodes).\nFixed JIT treating an array as packed after a string key write turned it into a hash.\nFixed bug GH-24436 (Tracing JIT: keep the SEND_VAL type guard after assigning to a reference).\nFixed bug GH-24745 (File cache loses attributes on constants on 32-bit builds).\nFixed bug GH-17733 (System entropy does not take into account function order, resulting in wrong functions possibly called in different configurations).\nFixed bug GH-24438 (Preserve indirect types in JIT side traces).\nFixed bug GH-24577 (CE-cache flag on interned class name visible before map_ptr offset).\nFixed tracing JIT losing register-allocated CVs when an interrupt is handled at the end of a loop trace.\nFixed bug GH-24675 (function with >~1.7 MB of machine code corrupts JIT buffer accounting).\nFixed JIT segfault on switch over a string reference holding a non-string value.\nFixed AArch64 JIT encoding of invalid logical immediates.\nFixed JIT crashes when handling a VM interrupt with a stale saved opline in the tailcall VM.\nFixed function JIT misinterpreting VM-enter results after an interrupt callback in the CALL and TAILCALL VMs.\nFixed unsound shift_left_overflows range when shift wraps.\nFixed bug GH-23572 (Tracing JIT calls the wrong method for self::/parent:: static calls in trait methods shared by several classes).\nFix block pass dropping ZEND_FAST_CALL OP2 definition.\nFixed bug GH-23626 (orphaned temporaries cause leaks and assertions).\nFix preloaded functions JIT-compiled on load being overwritten after restart.\nFix opcache.interned_strings_buffer being 0 in threads started later (ZTS).\nFixed potential infinite recursion/hang (HYBRID/TAILCALL respectively) when zend_interrupt_function resets EG(vm_interrupt).\nFix JIT losing the called scope of self::/parent:: calls in included files.\nFixed preloaded functions not JIT-compiled again after OPcache restart.\nFixed bug GH-24988 (Incorrect opcode range check causes bugs with exceptions in function JIT).\nFixed bug GH-22216 (spurious opcache.memory_consumption warning on each new ZTS thread; the directive is also reported as 0 in worker threads).\nFixed build and test compatibility with OpenSSL 4.0 and 4.1.\nFixed bug GH-24784 (openssl_pkcs7_read() and openssl_cms_read() overwrite certificates with CRLs).\nFixed invalid ATTR_ORACLE_NULLS values being accepted and truncated.\nFixed a duplicate warning when ATTR_STATEMENT_CLASS is rejected on a persistent connection.\nFixed constructor option errors naming argument #3 ($password) instead of argument #4 ($options).\nFixed bug GH-25006 (getColumnMeta() reads out of bounds for an out-of-range column index).\nFixed a use-after-free when a persistent connection receives a notice after the request that called Pdo\\Pgsql::setNoticeCallback() has ended.\nFixed bug GH-24990 (Statement unusable after a failed execute()).\nFixed bug GH-25093 (Phar::webPhar() redirect reads past the request URI).\nFixed bug GH-25089 (Heap buffer over-read via crafted alias size in zip-based phar).\nFixed bug GH-8469 (Phar::decompressFiles() and Phar::compressFiles() retain compressed contents after changing compression).\nFixed bug GH-24740 (Oversized tar metadata exhausts the memory limit).\nFixed bug GH-25090 (UAF in phar rename() of an entry with metadata).\nFixed bug GH-25091 (UAF in phar rename() when source and destination are equal).\nFixed bug GH-25092 (Double free in Phar::copy() on link and mounted entries).\nFixed bug GH-24531 (Crash when modifying a zip-based phar whose file was renamed).\nFixed GHSA-68fq-fh7h-f8gr (PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade). (CVE-2026-128090)\nFixed bug GH-22480 (Use-after-free when re-watching an already-watched variable).\nFixed over-read when watching a packed array element.\nFixed double free of watch element chains.\nFixed posix_setrlimit() rejecting POSIX_RLIMIT_INFINITY on Solaris.\nFixed a crash in readline_info() when completion_append_character contains a non-ASCII byte.\nFixed infinite loop in sapi_header_op() for headers of 4 GiB or more.\nFixed GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg (SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions). (CVE-2026-15353)\nFixed GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 (SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references). (CVE-2026-129506)\nValidate whole session ID instead of stopping at the first NUL byte.\nFixed GHSA-fm2m-fjf5-v3cp (Partially overwritten session files can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-126714)\nFixed GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx (Session serializer mismatch can lead to remote code execution). (CVE-2026-115560)\nFixed GHSA-g3vh-838c-65v7 (Use-after-free after interrupted session shutdown). (CVE-2026-129481)\nFixed bug GH-24264 (Unwind/GracefulExit discarded in spl_iterators.c).\nFixed bug GH-24748 (socket_set_option() crashes with declared object properties).\nFixed memory leaks in checkdnsrr() and dns_check_record() on Windows.\nFixed __unserialize() and __wakeup() being called for objects with a missing closing brace.\nFixed bug GH-24308 (Request shutdown calls closelog() even when syslog was not opened by PHP).\nFixed password_get_info() and password_needs_rehash() accepting malformed bcrypt costs.\nFixed proc_open() null descriptor not being inheritable on Windows.\nDon't share the unserialize() context with enum autoloaders.\nFixed bug GH-24399 (usleep() and time_nanosleep() ignore queued APCs on Windows).\nFixed glob() not negating bracket expressions that start with \"^\".\nFixed bug GH-24552 (Case-insensitive substr_compare(), ksort() and krsort() are still locale-dependent).\nFixed bug GH-24605 (var_export() crashes on deeply nested arrays and objects).\nFix use-after-free in Randomizer::shuffleArray() when the engine throws.\nFixed GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j (Mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext). (CVE-2026-128064)\nFixed GHSA-mmf9-xm3v-hg2x (Denial of service through folded HTTP response headers). (CVE-2026-127960)\nFixed bug GH-24508 (HTTP wrapper leaks the dechunk filter when header parsing fails after Transfer-Encoding).\nFixed bug GH-24509 (HTTP wrapper leaks Location buffer on empty Location header).\nFix out-of-bounds reads parsing ftp:// wrapper server replies.\nFixed tidy_repair_string(), tidy_repair_file(), tidy::repairString() and tidy::repairFile() rejecting null for $encoding.\nFixed bug GH-25019 (Uri\\Rfc3986\\Uri rejects a port with leading zeros as out of range).\nUpgrade to uriparser 1.0.3. (CVE-2026-48841)\nFixed GHSA-mg3p-mxj9-g2mm (Incorrect RFC 3986 URI serialization for oversized input). (CVE-2026-129438)\nFixed bug GH-25009 (GetConsoleTitleW() buffer size passed in bytes).\nFixed sapi_windows_cp_set() and sapi_windows_cp_conv() accepting a negative codepage on 32bit platforms.\nReject broken libzip versions 1.3.1, 1.7.0 and 1.12.0 during Windows configuration.\nE