      "body": "In StubGenerator::generate_base64_decodeBlock() (x86_64 AVX-512 VBMI path), L_finalBit handles 1-63 leftover bytes with a masked vector sequence that computes output_size = (len/4)*3. Valid inputs always have a length multiple of 4, so this bug triggers only on invalid inputs: with length < 4 (e.g. \"A\".repeat(64)+\"=\" leaves 1 byte after L_process64Loop), output_size starts at 0 and the padding path decrements it below zero, producing a wrong output_mask. The stub stores past the logical output length before returning to Java, corrupting the heap.\nThe suggested fix is to early-return to Java if length < 4.\nI confirm that I make this contribution in accordance with the OpenJDK Interim AI Policy.\nChange must not contain extraneous whitespace\nCommit message must refer to an issue\nChange must be properly reviewed (2 reviews required, with at least 1 Reviewer, 1 Author)\n⚠️ Failed to retrieve information on issue 8392044. Please make sure it exists and is accessible.\n⚠️ Failed to retrieve information on issue 8392044.\n$ git fetch https://git.openjdk.org/jdk.git pull/32781/head:pull/32781\nUpdate a local copy of the PR:\n$ git pull https://git.openjdk.org/jdk.git pull/32781/head\n$ git pr checkout 32781\nView PR using the GUI difftool:\n$ git pr show -t 32781\nDownload this PR as a diff file:",
