      "id": "bbc-2026-11-19-leftover-pumpkins-help-deliver-1-000th-free-meal",
      "title": "Leftover pumpkins help deliver 1,000th free meal",
      "summary": "\"It's a really tough time for a lot of people,\" a sustainable food organisation says.",
      "body": "Leftover pumpkins have helped a sustainable food organisation provide its 1,000th free meal to low-income households.Cambridge Sustainable Food started producing recipe kits earlier this year using fruit and vegetables that would have otherwise gone to waste.The group received masses of pumpkins from local farmers after Halloween, including about 300kg (661lb) of them from one supplier alone.Alex Vardill, from the organisation, said many of the meal kits had been received by families who sometimes struggled to access fresh produce.\"This has been a real help with improving that access at a time when food is really expensive,\" the 25-year-old said.\"They provide everything you need to make a meal in one bag, already measured out, with a recipe there in front of you.\"The kits are funded by Cambridge City Council and South Cambridgeshire District Council.They are distributed by food hubs – a mini-supermarket where anyone can go to access low-cost food – and other local organisations.",
