    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-18-joint-record-six-referee-errors-in-last-premier-league-weeke",
      "title": "Joint-record six referee errors in last Premier League weekend",
      "summary": "The Premier League's Key Match Incidents Panel rules there were six on-field errors in the last round of games - the joint-highest in one weekend.",
      "body": "When the KMI Panel sits down to vote there are two separate considerations.The first is on the decision of the referee, which is a basic judgement in law and the Premier League's expected interpretation.The second is on the potential VAR intervention. This takes into account what the referee has said, the available replay angles and the high bar for intervention.Incident 1: Thierno Barry put Everton in front against Coventry in the 61st minute, but there was a VAR check for a potential handball.KMI Panel vote: 2:3 incorrect on the field, but 5:0 no VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"On the balance of probability the ball did accidentally strike Barry's hand. However, the readily available footage did not provide conclusive evidence.\"Incident 2: Crystal Palace were awarded a penalty against Liverpool three minutes into stoppage time for a foul by Milos Kerkez on Dario Osorio. But was it just a clash of heads?KMI Panel vote: 0:5 incorrect on the field, but 5:0 no VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"A penalty was incorrect with the contact being inevitable. However, it was not a clear and obvious error.\"Incident 3: Ipswich were awarded a 72nd-minute penalty against Bournemouth for a foul by Lewis Cook on Abdoul Ouattara.KMI Panel vote: 1:4 incorrect on the field, but 4:1 no VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"Ouattara made a clear step across Cook who didn't make a challenge and the referee's decision to award a penalty was incorrect. However, it was not a clear and obvious error.\"Incident 4: Potential second yellow card for Bournemouth's Marcus Tavernier.KMI Panel vote: 2:3 incorrect on the field; no VAR intervention possible.What the KMI Panel said: \"There was a clear, deliberate action by Tavernier to delay the restart.\"Some of the most high-profile decisions from across the weekend have not yet featured.That is because they have been voted to be correct on the field and through VAR.Incident 1: Leeds United's Jayden Bogle caught Tottenham's Mathys Tel on high on his ankle. There was no VAR review for a red card.KMI Panel vote: 3:2 correct on the field and for the VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"The majority felt Bogle was looking to challenge with his right leg and his left leg came down on the back of Tel's ankle without the speed, force or intensity to be serious foul play. Two panellists felt that the challenge was sufficiently dangerous to merit a red card.\"Incident 2: Chelsea's Cole Palmer went down on the edge of the area under a challenge by Sunderland's Luke O'Nien.KMI Panel vote: 4:1 correct on the field and for the VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"Clear contact made by O'Nien on Palmer which the panel felt should have been penalised with a free-kick on the basis that contact was made outside the area. One panellist felt that the foul contact was inside the area.\"Incident 3: Sunderland were awarded a penalty when Levi Colwill was ruled to have tripped Brian Bobbey.KMI Panel vote: 5:0 correct on the field and for the VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"There was upper body holding from both players as they progressed into the penalty area before a careless trip by the Chelsea defender.\"Incident 4: Possible foul by Senne Lammens on Aston Villa goalkeeper Zion Suzuki before Patrick Dorgu's 96th-minute equaliser.KMI Panel vote: 5:0 correct on the field and for the VAR intervention.What the KMI Panel said: \"Although Lammens turned away from the ball, the contact he made on Suzuki was not impactful.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-18T12:38:38.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/d44c/live/1634e590-e345-11f1-99aa-0f40b013ad11.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c69q8jy924y4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
