      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-18-evidence-yc-s21-is-hiring",
      "title": "Evidence (YC S21) Is Hiring",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/evidence/jobs/1xb9PpP-founding-gtm-lead\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50545238\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Evidence is building the new standard for business intelligence, designed for a world where humans and AI agents work together on analytics.\nAt the foundation is Evidence Core, our open source framework for building reports and data products as code. On top of it, we're building Evidence Studio: a complete enterprise business intelligence platform combining an AI analytics agent with access control, enterprise security, and governance.\nThousands of organizations use Evidence, from startups to Fortune 100 companies. We've built a product people love, a substantial open source community, and a growing enterprise business.\nWe're now looking for someone to help us bring Evidence to a much larger audience.\nYou'll work directly with our cofounder and CEO to build Evidence's growth engine. We're a small team, and you'll have enormous ownership over how we reach new customers.\nOur goal is to build repeatable systems that consistently generate qualified opportunities for our team.\nThere's a lot to work with. Our large open source community (7,000+ GitHub stars) and growing customer base give you a head start: an established audience, a steady stream of new product capabilities, and interesting customer stories waiting to be told.\nSome of the things you'll work on:\nWriting and content: Create excellent technical articles, product explainers, emails, videos, and other content that helps people understand what Evidence can do.\nProduct marketing: Turn new features and product releases into compelling announcements, landing pages, and campaigns that drive adoption and demand.\nWeb and landing pages: Build and iterate on marketing pages, product pages, and campaign landing pages using AI coding tools, without depending on engineering for every change.\nCustomer stories: Work with our customers and sales team to turn interesting use cases into case studies, articles, and other marketing materials.\nDistribution and growth: Find creative ways to reach new audiences through social media, email, communities, events, and other channels, turning attention into qualified opportunities.\nMarketing infrastructure: Build and improve the systems we use to understand our audience, track engagement, run campaigns, and measure results, using AI and automation to work more effectively.\nYou'll be encouraged to experiment, measure results, and double down on what works. We care much more about generating real customer interest than producing perfect strategies.\nWe move quickly, and you'll start making an impact right away.\nFirst week: Get familiar with Evidence, meet some of our customers, and build something with our product. Publish your first piece of content.\nFirst two weeks: Ship your first product announcement or feature page, and start experimenting with distribution.\nFirst month: Launch your first end-to-end marketing campaign, from identifying an audience and crafting a message to distribution and measuring results.\nBy the end of your first month, you'll have shipped real work, learned from the results, and started building repeatable processes for reaching new customers.\nThe kind of person we're looking for\nYou're a great writer. You can explain technical ideas clearly, make them interesting, and persuade without resorting to marketing jargon. You have strong editorial judgment, care deeply about the quality of your work, and enjoy writing.\nYou're technically inclined. You don't need to be a software engineer, but you're comfortable using AI tools to build web pages and ship things yourself.\nYou have a bias toward getting things done. You'd rather build and ship something than spend weeks planning it.\nYou're analytical and commercially minded. You want to understand what drives customer acquisition, measure the results of your work, and continuously improve.\nYou're excited about the capabilities of AI and are constantly experimenting with new ways to move faster, without compromising on quality.\nYou're serious about building a career in marketing or GTM. You want to become exceptional at your craft, take on increasingly challenging work, and grow into greater ownership and responsibility. You're excited by the opportunity to help build a marketing function from the ground up.\nYou probably have 1–3 years of experience in marketing, ideally at a technical startup. But we care much more about your rate of learning, judgment, and what you can do than how long you've been doing it.\nThis is an opportunity to build a growth function from the ground up, working directly with the founders of a growing software company.\nIf this sounds like you, we'd like to hear from you.\nEvidence is the leading BI-as-code platform and the best way to run business intelligence with AI agents.\nEvidence Core is the most popular framework for building reports, decision support tools, and dashboards with code. It powers analytics at thousands of organizations, including several Fortune 100 companies.\nEvidence Studio is a complete enterprise business intelligence platform built around Evidence Core, combining an AI analytics agent with access control, enterprise security, and governance. Evidence Studio powers analytics at hundreds of organizations.\nEvidence was founded in 2021 by Sean Hughes and Adam McAskill. Prior to founding Evidence, Sean and Adam built the data science team at Canada's leading private equity fund.\nEvidence is venture-backed, with support from leading institutions and angels, including Y Combinator, SV Angel, A Capital, Tristan Handy (founder of dbt), and Andrew Miklas (founder of PagerDuty and YC partner).Evidence is the leading BI-as-code platform and the best way to run business intelligence with AI agents.\nEvidence Core is the most popular framework for building reports, decision support tools, and dashboards with code. It powers analytics at thousands of organizations, including several Fortune 100 companies.\nEvidence Studio is a complete enterprise business intelligence platform built around Evidence Core, combining an AI analytics agent with access control, enterprise security, and governance. Evidence Studio powers analytics at hundreds of organizations.\nEvidence was founded in 2021 by Sean Hughes and Adam McAskill. Prior to founding Evidence, Sean and Adam built the data science team at Canada’s leading private equity fund.\nEvidence is venture-backed, with support from leading institutions and angels, including Y Combinator, SV Angel, A Capital, Tristan Handy (founder of dbt), and Andrew Miklas (founder of PagerDuty and YC partner).",
