      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-tech-life",
      "title": "Tech Life",
      "summary": "Video gaming is huge - it's more lucrative than the movies and music combined.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsWorld Service,·17 Nov 2026,·26 minsDoes the gaming industry have a climate problem?Tech LifeAvailable for over a yearMillions of us play on consoles, laptops and phones - it's big business. Grand Theft Auto 6 is the latest blockbuster release. But is gaming having an impact on the environment?\nOur BBC World Service colleagues at The Climate Question have been looking at gaming and the effect it has on the climate. Jordan Dunbar presents the latest edition, and he joins us on Tech Life to talk about the issues.\nAlso in this episode, we hear from the huge Chinese tech company Tencent about their investment plans. And we find out about the specialised computer chip designed to process AI on your devices.\nProducer: Tom Quinn and Imran Rahman-Jones\n(Photo: In the foreground a gamer holds a games console controller. In the background a car video game is displayed on a large monitor. Credit: Getty Images)Programme WebsiteMore episodes",
