      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-17-mai-code-2-and-code-2-flash",
      "title": "MAI Code 2 and Code 2 Flash",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-code-2-and-mai-code-2-flash/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50535885\nPoints: 264\n# Comments: 123",
      "body": "Performance and speed for everyday coding\nMAI Code 2 is at the frontier of price-performance for common enterprise coding tasks and excels in taking code to production, deep debugging, multi-file implementation, repo wide reasoning, and UI. It does all of this while also delivering changes code maintainers would merge, at a fraction of frontier cost.\nMeanwhile, MAI Code 2 Flash is designed for high-volume work such as code explanations, targeted edits, routine fixes, and rapid iterations, while bringing quality at a much lower cost.\nProduction quality at less than half the price\nTo deliver the best price-performance, we’ve built these models to prioritize the coding work our customers do every day. They’re explicitly not yet tuned for harder problems, like fundamental science research and very long horizon agentic work.\nAveraged over four widely used benchmarks that target the everyday enterprise coding tasks we see in GitHub Copilot (DeepSWE 1.1, Terminal Bench 2.1, SWE-Atlas and FrontierCode v1.1), MAI Code 2 gives you 98% of the performance of GPT 6.1 Sol at 40% of the cost, and 96% of Claude Opus 5.5’s performance at just 5% of the cost.1\nMAI Code 2 is also tuned for producing great dashboards and visualizations, and excels at visual coding. In blind frontend app evaluations, reviewers preferred its results over GPT-6 Sol 64% of the time.2\nIn addition, MAI Code 2 Flash offers comparable performance to GPT-6 Luna and Claude Haiku 5.5 at 65% and 20% of the cost, across three coding benchmarks measuring day-to-day, high-volume routine coding tasks.3",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "lemonish97",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T18:25:13.000Z",
