      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-dechambeau-joins-dp-world-tour-after-liv-golf-collapse",
      "title": "DeChambeau joins DP World Tour after LIV Golf collapse",
      "summary": "American superstar Bryson DeChambeau is among a number of former LIV players who will play on the European-based DP World Tour next season.",
      "body": "Two-time US Open champion Bryson DeChambeau has agreed to join the DP World Tour for next season.DeChambeau was among a host of star names who joined LIV Golf four years ago and maintained his commitment even after Saudi Arabia's Public Investment Fund withdrew its financial backing for the breakaway tour in April.Earlier this month the 33-year-old American said he \"gave everything\" to keep LIV Golf alive as the tour confirmed its intention to wind down operations.As first reported in the Telegraph,, external DeChambeau successfully submitted his application to join the European Tour before Sunday's deadline.DeChambeau has already confirmed he will compete in Gary Player's Nedbank Golf Challenge - a DP World Tour event - in South Africa in December.As a recent major champion DeChambeau has been given 'category one' membership by the DP World Tour, which means he is guaranteed entry to any event across the season.Dustin Johnson, Cameron Smith and Bubba Watson - other former major champions who defected to LIV - have signed agreements to receive invitations to a specific number of tournaments.Veteran English trio Ian Poulter, Lee Westwood and Paul Casey, plus Northern Ireland's Graeme McDowell, are among a number of ex-LIV players who are eligible to play on the DP World Tour in 2027.The full-time return of Spain's Jon Rahm and England's Tyrrell Hatton, who did not resign their memberships, has also been confirmed. \"There has been significant change in the landscape of men's professional golf over the past 12 months,\" said DP World Tour chief executive Guy Kinnings.\"As golf's global tour, we have taken a pragmatic approach to this unique and unprecedented situation as we go into next year, always with the best interests of our entire membership at the forefront of our minds.\"As one of the poster boys of LIV Golf, and one of the biggest names in the sport, it was intriguing to see what DeChambeau would do next.With LIV golfers automatically banned for a year by the PGA Tour, it was thought he might decide to focus on his YouTube and social media channels - which have attracted a new, younger audience of many millions - over the next 12 months.But joining the DP World Tour is a logical option for the big-hitting American, who reportedly received £95m, external to join LIV in 2022 and earned almost £50m in prize money over four seasons.Signing up for the European-based tour means he can play the traditional format of the game on a regular basis and offers a pathway back to the PGA Tour.The leading 10 players on the DP World Tour in a season are guaranteed PGA Tour cards for the following season, which was a route taken by Patrick Reed - DeChambeau's former US Ryder Cup team-mate - when he left LIV before the start of the 2026 season.For the DP World Tour, DeChambeau brings further star power to their product.DeChambeau will join the likes of European superstars Rory McIlroy and Tommy Fleetwood as full-time members, and boosts the tour's stock as the golfing landscape continues to realign following LIV's demise.\"I think a name like Bryson DeChambeau and everything he brings with him, good and bad, he brings eyeballs, which is a good thing for tournaments,\" McIlroy said earlier this month.Six-time major champion McIlroy also claimed those connected to LIV were expressing an ambition to \"destroy the European Tour\" during this year's Masters.Instead, the Saudi-backed venture is to be liquidated and has led to an influx of big-names joining the DP World Tour.As well as DeChambeau being given membership for the first time, it was announced that Johnson, Smith and Watson are among a group of nine former LIV players allowed to play a limited number of events.They will be picked at the discretion of the DP World Tour to \"add value to those tournaments\", which is designed to prevent full-time members from missing playing opportunities.On allowing former LIV players to join the tour, Kinnings added: \"We realise there are different viewpoints.\"But this approach, discussed and agreed with our tournament committee and allied to this responsibly managed programme of invites, will add value which, in turn, will benefit the tour as a whole.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T13:44:17.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/df39/live/f1a6c4a0-e277-11f1-ad71-0bc71faa76c4.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/golf/articles/c5vg27yzm9exo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 3,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-channel-4-admits-it-doesn-t-know-number-of-married-at-first-",
      "title": "Channel 4 admits it doesn't know number of Married At First Sight UK sex abuse complaints",
      "summary": "C4's chief executive is questioned by MPs after a string of allegations were made about the show.",
      "body": "Married at First Sight UK, known as MAFS UK, had been running for 10 seasons and was one of Channel 4's biggest shows, with audience figures often topping three million.The Panorama investigation in May heard from three women who made allegations about the men they were partnered with - claims the men deny:One woman said her on-screen husband raped her and threatened her with an acid attack.A second woman told both Channel 4 and production company CPL, before broadcast, about being allegedly raped by her on-screen husband. Her episodes were still aired.A third woman accused her on-screen husband of sexual misconduct.All three women accused the show of not doing enough to protect them.A review was commissioned into MAFS UK by Channel 4 shortly after the BBC first contacted the broadcaster with details of the allegations.Earlier this month, the completed review recommended extra safeguards on the show. But Channel 4 said the programme had \"run its course\" and apologised to the women involved in the investigation.Speaking to MPs on the House of Commons culture and media committee on Tuesday, Dogra was repeatedly asked if she knew how many allegations Channel 4 and CPL had received over the years that MAFS UK was on air.\"I looked specifically into those instances [the three women], I did not do a broad sweep of every episode or every season of the show. That is not what the terms of reference for the show were,\" she responded.\"If there are others, we would take them seriously and look into them on the same basis.\"Channel 4's bosses were also questioned at length about Brand by MPs in the hearing.Brand's work on Channel 4 included hosting Big Brother sister show Big Brother's Big Mouth and its celebrity equivalent from 2004 to 2007, a chat show in 2006, and appearing on Big Fat Quiz of the Year.Addressing Dogra and Channel 4's chairman Geoff Cooper, MPs said the member of staff who made two complaints about Brand \"fell through the cracks\".In response, Dogra said: \"I'm not sure we can apologise enough as an organisation for putting her through that twice. We have apologised in public in the past and in private.\"She accepted that the woman's complaints were \"not handled properly\" and added that \"it's almost unforgivable that happened twice\".When asked by the committee if junior members of staff could raise complaints against a star without fear of losing their job, Dogra replied she \"can't say 100%\" that that would be the case.Woman who accuses Russell Brand of rape says prison message 'upsetting'\"What I can do is set the standard, set the tone, make sure that the facilities are available, make sure that my staff and the production companies understand the repercussions of not complying, and understand the kind of culture that I'm trying to set, and we're trying to set as an industry.\"She also said she found the \"cultural personality\" around Brand \"horrendous\".\"I find it distasteful, and I look at the jokes... that is the lowest form of humour, because these are jokes that are made at the expense of someone else's physical safety.\"I don't believe it should have been acceptable then, and I certainly don't think it's acceptable now.\"During the session, Dame Caroline also put to Channel 4 bosses that in both the MAFS UK and Brand cases, the broadcaster appeared like \"a child with their hand in the cookie jar\".The committee chairwoman asked: \"To what extent can you reassure us that Channel 4's priority is genuinely the welfare of the staff who work there, the staff who have worked there, and the people who take part in your shows - rather than purely when the world is looking at you and you suddenly feel that you've got a reputational reason to take a look at these shows?\"Dogra responded by saying that when Channel 4 commissioned the review, \"we didn't even know whether the Panorama programme would be made\".She added: \"We had received a right-to-reply letter and the programme came out six weeks later, but it equally it could not have been made. We always intended to do the review.\"In the instance of the woman who tried to complain about Brand, she added: \"I'm not sure there are more apologies we can give. Because none of those things should've happened.\"If you have more information about this story, you can reach Noor by email at noor.nanji@bbc.co.uk",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T13:43:49.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/0a4e/live/c621a3a0-5603-11f1-ad45-8ffb2d2085e2.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqvg2xvdpy2ro?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 4,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-bethell-to-have-more-surgery-and-miss-south-africa-tour",
      "title": "Bethell to have more surgery and miss South Africa tour",
      "summary": "Jacob Bethell will miss England’s Test tour of South Africa because he requires more surgery on the knee injury that has kept him out since July.",
      "body": "Jacob Bethell will miss England's Test tour of South Africa because he requires more surgery on the knee injury that has kept him out since July.Batter Bethell was due to make his return in the ongoing white-ball tour of Australia, but had to leave that trip at the weekend after suffering what England described as a \"setback\" in training.The 23-year-old has met with a specialist and, as first reported by the Telegraph, will have a second operation on his right knee.He has also been released by Indian Premier League side Royal Challengers Bengaluru (RCB).With no timeframe placed on Bethell's recovery, RCB director of cricket Mo Bobat said the decision to part ways was influenced by doubts over the England batter's fitness for the 2027 IPL season, beginning in March.The likely long-term nature of Bethell's recovery means he is a major doubt for England's winter beyond the South Africa tour - two Tests in Bangladesh in February and the one-off 150th anniversary day-night Test against Australia in Melbourne in March.It could mean that he now does not play again until the summer, in the build-up to a home Ashes series.England are yet to confirm Bethell's replacement for the three Tests against South Africa. They will choose from the England Lions, who arrive in South Africa before the Test squad.When the Warwickshire man missed the three Tests against Pakistan during the home summer, his place in the England squad went to Ollie Pope.Bethell has not played since the third one-day international against India at Lord's in July, when he suffered discomfort in his knee.In his absence from the Test side during the Pakistan series, Emilio Gay opened and Jordan Cox took Bethell's slot at number three.It was expected that one of Gay or Cox would have to drop out of the starting XI in South Africa to make way for Bethell's return.When England announced their touring squad last week, selector Marcus North said that no decisions had been made on the make-up of the first-choice top six.Now, in Bethell's continued absence, Gay and Cox will have further opportunities to make claims for a long-term place in the Test side.Surrey's Pope has not played for England since the third Ashes Test against Australia in Adelaide in December of last year.He was due to be with the Lions in South Africa on a tour that overlaps with the Test series and appears the most likely candidate to replace Bethell.If England opt against Pope, Somerset's James Rew and uncapped Durham opener Ben McKinney have both been in strong form on the Lions' recent white-ball tour of the West Indies.This latest setback is a significant blow to Bethell, who looked to have cemented his place in the Test side with a sparkling century in the final Ashes Test in Sydney in January.But the knee injury cut short his summer, meaning he missed The Hundred, the Pakistan series, white-ball matches against Sri Lanka, then the limited-overs tours of Pakistan and Australia.England are already without Josh Tongue for the first Test against South Africa in Johannesburg, beginning on 17 December. The pace bowler will be at home for the birth of his second child.North has previously confirmed that England will call on fast-bowling reserves from the Lions to cover for Tongue.",
