      "id": "bbc-2026-11-17-blackburn-boss-mowbray-steps-back-over-health-issues",
      "title": "Blackburn boss Mowbray steps back over health issues",
      "summary": "Blackburn Rovers head coach Tony Mowbray steps back from his role with the Championship club due to health issues.",
      "body": "Blackburn Rovers head coach Tony Mowbray has stepped back from his role with the Championship club amid health issues.The 62-year-old returned for a second spell in June having previously spent five years managing Rovers between 2017 and 2022.Mowbray had previously taken time out of the game during his time as Birmingham City boss in early 2024 following a health scare, and later revealed he had been undergoing treatment for bowel cancer.Rovers said Damien Johnson and Mike Dodds would take responsibility for first-team duties \"for the time being\".BBC Sport was initially told Mowbray had \"stepped down\" but we have since been updated that he has \"stepped back\". No further details have been given although the club are not thought to be looking for a successor.\"Unfortunately, due to health issues, I have to step back from my role as head coach of Blackburn Rovers,\" Mowbray said in a statement., external\"I'm immensely proud of this group of players. Their dedication and professionalism have given us some memorable performances and wins, and I've loved working with them.\"Thank you to my coaching staff for all your hard work and for the support you've given me. It's been a pleasure working alongside you.\"To the fans, thank you for the way you've supported me and the team this season. I've always tried to give you a team that you can be proud of. Your support has meant a great deal to me.\"Mowbray has transformed Blackburn this season, after a they hovered around the relegation places for much of last term before eventually finishing 20th in the Championship and five points above the drop zone.They are currently 13th in the Championship table having won six of their 15 league games and three points outside the play-offs.The announcement comes before Sunday's Lancashire derby against Burnley at Turf Moor, which was set to be Mowbray's 900th game in management as well as his 63rd birthday.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
