      "id": "bbc-2026-11-16-burnham-urges-caution-on-scrapping-3pm-tv-blackout",
      "title": "Burnham urges caution on scrapping 3pm TV blackout",
      "summary": "Andy Burnham urges caution on lifting the Saturday 3pm TV blackout in the UK, saying the health of the football pyramid should come first.",
      "body": "Andy Burnham has urged caution on lifting the Saturday 3pm TV blackout in the UK, saying the health of the football pyramid should come first.The rule was introduced in the 1960s to encourage fans to attend lower league games and prevents matches from being shown on UK television between 2:45pm and 5:15pm on Saturdays.The blackout, which is enforced by Article 48 of the Uefa Statutes and is imposed by the English and Scottish football associations, comes into effect when 50% of fixtures in the top two divisions are scheduled to kick off at 3pm.The Premier League is in the middle of a record £6.7bn domestic TV deal for Sky and TNT to show up to 270 live games a season. But there could be room for change with the 3pm rule in the upcoming broadcast cycle, as the rights deals for the Premier League, EFL and SPFL all end in 2028-29.The prime minister said any decision to remove the ban would require careful thought about the consequences.\"I would urge a bit of caution [on the blackout], because it does protect the income of lower-league clubs,\" Burnham said.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
