      "id": "bbc-2026-11-16-thrift-shop-asks-shoppers-to-nominate-a-charity",
      "title": "Thrift shop asks shoppers to nominate a charity",
      "summary": "The owners want customers and donors to decide what charities benefit each month.",
      "body": "Shoppers and donors at a new charity shop will be able to help decide which organisations benefit from the money it raises.Twisted Sisters Thrift Store, in Tunstall opened last week, and is inviting customers to nominate causes they would like to support, with a different charity set to receive donations each month.Owner Julie Rindam said the idea came after the closure of a charity shop; she had run for eight years.\"The pastor is retiring and it was either another empty shop or I took it on.\"Rindam said many of the shop's regular donors wanted to continue supporting charitable causes, leading to the idea of allowing the community to decide where the money goes.\"All my donators still wanted to drop off to us, so we thought, well, how about a different charity every month?\" she said.\"We ask all the donators who they'd like us to donate to, so every month it will be a different charity benefiting.\"Rather than supporting a single organisation, the shop plans to keep a record of suggestions, being completely transparent with customers and donors before selecting a charity at the end of each month.\"Everyone who drops off, we ask and we keep a book and every month we'll pick a different charity to benefit from, whether that's City Dogs Home, Cancer Research, Diabetes or other charities,\" Rindam said.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
