      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-16-coles-hit-by-a-cybersecurity-incident",
      "title": "Coles hit by a cybersecurity incident",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.colesgroup.com.au/updates/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50512824\nPoints: 65\n# Comments: 45",
      "body": "Current as at 16 November 2026, 8:30am\nColes Group Limited is currently investigating a cyber security incident.\nBased on the findings of our investigation to date, we have not identified any evidence that customer, team or supplier data has been compromised or removed from Coles’ systems.\nColes is working with the Australian Cyber Security Centre and will continue to engage with appropriate agencies and regulators as investigations continue.\nColes is also working with global cyber security experts to contain and secure the Coles IT environment.\nOperations continue and customers are able to shop as normal with Coles in stores and online.\nWe apologise for any concern this may cause our customers and key stakeholders at a time of increasing cyber incidents in Australia and around the world. We will provide further updates as appropriate on this page.",
