      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-16-tor-project-issues-rapid-response-dos-defense-fix-amid-susta",
      "title": "Tor Project Issues Rapid-Response DoS-Defense Fix Amid Sustained DDoS Attack",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://forum.torproject.org/t/security-release-0-4-9-17/22454\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50512441\nPoints: 65\n# Comments: 10",
      "body": "Below are the major changes of the released versions and links to more detailed release notes.\nToday, we are releasing 0.4.9.17, which includes a series of security fixes. One fix in particular is especially important for relay DoS defenses related to IPv6 handling.\nThis release comes in rapid response to the ongoing DDoS attack on the network, which has affected most relay operators. This is not an easy problem to address, as relays across the network are being overwhelmed by a massive flood of client circuits. We are actively evaluating additional defenses and so expect further releases in the near future.\nWe want to extend a huge thank you to all relay operators who have been helping us deal with this ongoing attack. The tor-relays@ mailing list has been very active and we are very grateful for your time, effort, and support. Please, continue doing so!\nIf you run a relay, please upgrade as soon as possible. No action item is required after upgrading.\nThank you to all… except our attacker(s).",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "aillia",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-16T00:21:54.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://forum.torproject.org/uploads/default/original/2X/d/d3424bed34f4ec18b2e99178c2801ba6dfb655d6.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://forum.torproject.org/t/security-release-0-4-9-17/22454",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
