      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-15-webgl-flight-simulator-with-seed-generated-terrain",
      "title": "WebGL Flight Simulator with seed generated terrain",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://baron.by.dai.studio/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50510296\nPoints: 192\n# Comments: 46",
      "body": "Take off. Explore. Land it in one piece.\nFlyLeft thumb: drag anywhere on the left half (drag down to climb)\nThrottleLever on the right edge (double-tap = idle)\nFlapsFLAP + / FLAP − (UP, T/O, LAND)\nRudderAutomatic (the stick steers on the ground)\nBail outHold BAIL for a second\nTiltPause → Steer by tilting\nPitchW / S or ↑ / ↓ (S pulls up)\nRollA / D or ← / →\nThrottleShift / Ctrl (or 1–9, 0 = full)\nFlapsF more / V less (UP, T/O, LAND)\nDestination← / → on the menu (Cross-country)\nPause / RestartEsc or P / R\nGamepadL-stick fly, R-stick X rudder / Y throttle\n← → category · ↑ ↓ choose · drag to look around · Esc back\nTap a tab and a card · drag the plane to look around\nYour browser or graphics driver doesn't support WebGL 2. Try the latest Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari, and make sure hardware acceleration is turned on.\nThe browser reset the graphics context. Hang on, restoring…",
