      "id": "bbc-2026-11-15-fifth-canadian-soldier-dies-from-injuries-caused-by-large-fi",
      "title": "Fifth Canadian soldier dies from injuries caused by large fire at military base",
      "summary": "Pte William Douglas Dal Bianco died from his injuries on Friday, a month after a fire that tore through CFB Wainwright.",
      "body": "Members of 1 Canadian Mechanized Brigade Group had been conducting live-fire training at the base, in the province of Alberta, when the fire broke out.Military officials said at the time that the fire spread across a kilometre in a matter of seconds, taking many of those on the base by surprise.Firefighters battled the blaze through the night, while nearby hospitals became inundated by injured personnel and staff.Carney described it as \"one of the worst tragedies for the forces on Canadian soil in peacetime\". An investigation found that the fire was likely sparked by a grenade launcher being fired on the base's grenade range, officials said. Firefighters on the base had known about the fire but could not tackle it because it was in a danger area that could contain unspent explosives.Canadian Chief of the Defence Staff Gen Jennie Carignan said the nation's armed forces were \"heartbroken\" by the loss of Dal Bianco, while Defence Minister David McGuinty offered his \"deepest condolences\" to his family, friends and colleagues.\"No words can ease the pain of losing a loved one, and my thoughts remain with all those affected by this tragedy,\" he said. \"We remain committed to supporting the families and the Canadian Armed Forces community during this profoundly difficult time, and to honouring Private Dal Bianco's service, dedication and sacrifice to Canada.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
