      "id": "techcrunch-2026-11-14-tesla-opens-cybercab-pre-orders-for-personal-use-with-geo-re",
      "title": "Tesla opens Cybercab pre-orders ‘for personal use,’ with geo restrictions and a $299 monthly fee",
      "summary": "12:04 PM PST · November 14, 2026 Image Credits:Josh Edelson / AFP / Getty Images Tesla said on Friday evening that “select customers” now have the opportunity to pre-order the company’s autonomous, golden Cybercab “for personal use.” More details became clear as those select customers looked at the order page. Tech reviewer Marques Brownlee posted that buyers “must accept deliv…",
      "body": "12:04 PM PST · November 14, 2026\nImage Credits:Josh Edelson / AFP / Getty Images\nTesla said on Friday evening that “select customers” now have the opportunity to pre-order the company’s autonomous, golden Cybercab “for personal use.”\nMore details became clear as those select customers looked at the order page. Tech reviewer Marques Brownlee posted that buyers “must accept delivery” in one of a handful of Texas cities and that the Cybercab will only operate in certain geofenced areas. The estimated delivery date is December 2026.\nIn addition to the $29,990 price tag, Cybercab owners will need to pay $299 per month to operate their vehicle.\nIn response to Brownlee’s post, Tesla CEO Elon Musk said the Cybercab “will be available nationwide, as we receive regulatory approval.” He added that the monthly fee is “too high”: “Should match the cost of Tesla [Full Self-Driving] and connectivity for other models, which is more like ~$115/month.”\nTesla’s Ashok Elluswamy offered more information about the geofencing, saying that Cybercab will work “unsupervised inside all the same geo locations as @robotaxi, just serving the owners’ needs.”\nAfter falling far short of projected sales, Tesla recently announced it will cease Cybertruck production next year and use the additional factory capacity to build more Cybercabs.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Anthony Ha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-14T20:04:44.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tesla-cybercab-getty.jpg?resize=1200,834",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/14/tesla-opens-cybercab-pre-orders-for-personal-use-with-geo-restrictions-and-a-299-monthly-fee/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
