      "id": "theverge-2026-11-14-here-are-our-favorite-deals-from-rei-s-giant-holiday-sale",
      "title": "Here are our favorite deals from REI’s giant Holiday Sale",
      "summary": "Black Friday has become a shopping season of its own, with retailers once again offering discounts well ahead of the actual shopping holiday. We’ve already rounded up some of the best early Black Friday deals we’ve come across, but if you’re looking to save on outdoor gear or pick up something for an upcoming trip, REI’s annual Holiday Sale, which runs through November 23rd, is worth checking out.",
      "body": "Black Friday has become a shopping season of its own, with retailers once again offering discounts well ahead of the actual shopping holiday. We’ve already rounded up some of the best early Black Friday deals we’ve come across, but if you’re looking to save on outdoor gear or pick up something for an upcoming trip, REI’s annual Holiday Sale, which runs through November 23rd, is worth checking out.\nAs usual, the outdoor retailer is offering discounts on everything from smartwatches to camping equipment. In some cases, we’re seeing some of the lowest prices we’ve seen on our favorite wearables, including Garmin’s Forerunner 570, while gadgets like the InReach Mini 3 are also receiving sizable discounts. REI members can also use promo code HOLIDAY2026 to save 20 percent on one full-price item, plus an additional 20 percent on one REI Outlet item.\nTo save you time, we’ve sifted through the deluge of discounts to find an assortment of deals we recommend here at The Verge. We’ve also noted when competing retailers are offering lower prices on the same items, so you can be sure you’re getting the best deal possible.\nREI Siesta Hooded 20 Sleeping Bag\nMpowerd Luci Solar String Lights: Color\nGarmin InReach Mini 3 Plus\n[Product: Garmin Forerunner 570 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8R2BSKK/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgarmin-forerunner-570-gps-smartwatch-47-mm-aluminum-slate-gray-aluminum-2025%2FJXF9YFFYHJ%2Fsku%2F6633091, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC01097%2Fgarmin-forerunner-570]\n[Product: Garmin Venu 4 | https://www.amazon.com/Garmin-Advanced-Smartwatch-Flashlight-Periwinkle/dp/B0FRGFDWDQ?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fgarmin-venu-4-gps-smartwatch-41-mm-fiber-reinforced-polymer-lunar-gold-2025%2FJXF9YF5F6Z%2Fsku%2F6646700, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC05423%2Fgarmin-venu-4]\n* REI, Amazon, and Best Buy are also selling the Garmin Lily 2 Active for $249.99 ($50 off), which is its lowest price to date. The stylish smartwatch is a great budget-friendly Garmin, especially for people with smaller wrists. Like the standard Lily 2, it offers basic fitness tracking, notifications, and up to five days of battery life; however, the so-called “Active” model adds a physical button, built-in GPS, and support for more sports tracking. Read our Lily 2 review.\n* The Garmin Vivoactive 6 has returned to its all-time low of $249.99 ($50 off) at Amazon, Walmart, and REI. The fitness watch offers up to 11 days of battery life and tracks a range of workouts, including walking, running, cycling, HIIT, golf, and more. It also provides extensive health monitoring, including wrist-based heart rate detection, menstrual cycle and pregnancy tracking, and a customizable morning report that summarizes helpful health-related info. However, it lacks ECG compatibility, though it does have a slightly slimmer profile than its predecessor.\n[Product: Garmin Fenix 8 | https://www.amazon.com/Garmin-f%25C4%2593nix%25C2%25AE-Multisport-Long-Lasting-Built/dp/B0DD64SSJS?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2Ff-nix-8-51-mm-AMOLED-Slate-Gray-with-Black-Silicone-Band%2F11453103355, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F245469%2Fgarmin-fenix-8-amoled-sapphire]\n* The Wahoo Kickr V6 Smart Trainer is on sale at REI for $679.99 ($170 off). Like the more affordable Kickr Core 2 we covered in July, the Kickr V6 turns your existing bike into an indoor exercise bike, with Wi-Fi and Bluetooth connectivity for pairing with apps like Zwift. However, the higher-end trainer offers up to 2,200W of resistance and can replicate inclines of up to 20 percent, compared to the Core 2’s 1,800W and 16 percent. It also provides more accurate power measurements and is designed so that indoor rides feel more natural.\n[Product: EcoFlow Rapid Magnetic Power Bank | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F256047%2Fecoflow-rapid-magnetic-power-bank-10000-mah]\n* If you own an older iPhone with a Lightning port, you can grab InfinityLab’s InstantGo 10,000 Power Bank&nbsp;&nbsp;for&nbsp;&nbsp;$41.93 (about $28 off) at REI. The portable battery features a 10,000mAh capacity and a built-in Lightning cable, making it a solid all-in-one option for days when you won’t be near an outlet. It also supports passthrough charging, so you can charge your phone and the power bank at the same time.\n* DJI’s Osmo Mobile 8 is on sale for around $128.99 ($21 off) at REI, Amazon, and Best Buy, which is $10 shy of its best price to date. The smartphone gimbal supports 360-degree horizontal rotation and Apple’s DockKit, which allows the gimbal to track and follow pets and people across a wider range of camera apps. This discounted Advanced Tracking Combo also includes a multifunctional module for tracking people and pets, as well as a built-in tripod and extension rod that make it easier to film yourself without someone behind the camera.\n[Product: Soundcore Liberty 5 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DT4F2NM9?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2Fsoundcore-Liberty-5-Anker-Noise-Cancelling-Wireless-Earbuds-2x-Stronger-Voice-Reduction-Adaptive-Noise-Cancellation-Fast-Charging-Dolby-Audio-6-Mic-A%2F16405323935, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC05056%2Fsoundcore-by-anker-liberty-5-active-noise-canceling-wireless-earbuds%3Fcolor%3DBLACK]\n* You can buy Soundcore’s AeroFit 2 for $79.99 ($20 off) at REI, Amazon, and Best Buy, which is $2 shy of their lowest price to date. Their open-ear design lets you listen to music while staying vigilant in your surroundings; they also feature adjustable ear hooks for a secure fit, IP55 water and dust resistance, and up to 42 hours of battery life with the included charging case.\n[Product: Anker Nebula P1 projector | https://www.amazon.com/soundcore-Portable-Projector-Detachable-Adjustment/dp/B0FQL6HLQ3/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/101881227/type/dlg/https://www.soundcore.com/products/d2431-nebula-p1-portable-projector-with-detachable-speakers?variant=45904637198511, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC12612%2Fnebula-nebula-p1-projector-with-google-tv-projector-and-detachable-speakers]\n[Product: Garmin InReach Mini 3 Plus | https://www.amazon.com/Garmin-Satellite-Communicator-Touchscreen-Messaging/dp/B0G4RST8LV?tag=theverge02-20, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC06373%2Fgarmin-inreach-mini-3-plus, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/101881227/type/dlg/https://www.garmin.com/en-US/p/1756582/]\n* Garmin’s base InReach Mini 3 is available from REI, Amazon, and Garmin for around $349 ($100 off), nearly matching its lowest price to date. Like the Mini 2, the rugged, palm-sized satellite communicator lets you send texts, share your location, check the weather, and trigger SOS alerts when you’re off the grid, all while offering battery life that can outlast your average smartphone. Unlike the prior version, though, it features a color touchscreen, which makes it easier to navigate menus and bang out messages.\n* Garmin’s InReach Messenger Plus is also on sale at REI, Amazon, and direct from Garmin for $299.99 ($100 off), matching its best price to date. The subscription-based Plus model provides satellite connectivity and access to emergency services like the aforementioned InReach Mini 3, except it can also send photos and audio clips in addition to standard text messages.\n* The Chapter MIPS Bike Helmet is on sale starting at around $112.39 ($41 off) at REI, which nearly matches its best price to date. The lightweight helmet features a hidden PopLock for securing it with a U-lock or chain. It also has a sleek visor and a Micro-USB taillight with 30 lumens of brightness, one that automatically turns on when magnetically attached to the helmet.\n* Garmin’s Varia RTL515 Radar Taillight is on sale at REI and Amazon for $149.99 ($50 off), which is about $10 less than its all-time low. The headlight combines a bright LED light with a rearview radar that, when paired with a compatible device, warns you of cars approaching from behind from up to 153 yards away.\n[Product: BCA Tracker 3 Plus Avalanche Transceiver | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F182524%2Fbackcountry-access-tracker3-avalanche-transceiver%3Fcolor%3DBLACK]\n[Product: Exped MegaMat Duo | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F238244%2Fexped-megamat-duo-sleeping-pad%3Fsku%3D2382440001%26CAWELAID%3D120217890019006286, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F238244%2Fexped-megamat-duo-sleeping-pad%3Fsku%3D2382440001%26CAWELAID%3D120217890019006286, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F238244%2Fexped-megamat-duo-sleeping-pad%3Fsku%3D2382440001%26CAWELAID%3D120217890019006286]\n* A small chair is nice to have for lounging by the campfire, and REI’s Flexlite Camp Chair is a great option now that it’s down to&nbsp;&nbsp;around $67.39 (about $22 off) in multiple colors at REI. It features an aluminum frame, a stable four-leg design, and a ripstop polyester seat with water and stain resistance. When you’re done, it also folds down quickly into a drawstring bag, so you can throw it in your car.\n[Product: Kelty Low Loveseat | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F186918%2Fkelty-low-loveseat, https://www.avantlink.com/click.php?tt=cl&merchant_id=b5770911-39dc-46ac-ba0f-b49dbb30c5c7&website_id=f5f1e4bc-3964-4b83-993d-dc0307430171&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fb%2Fkelty-low-love-camp-chair%2F]\n* REI is currently selling its Magma 30 Sleeping Bag in a variety of sizes starting at $243.93 ($105 off). The bag uses 850-fill-power, water-resistant down for warmth and weighs under 20 ounces, depending on the size, making it a great budget pick if you’re looking to get into ultralight backpacking. It also includes a hood to help retain heat, extra room around the feet, and a terrific zipper design that’s less likely to snag when you’re crawling in or out.\n[Product: REI Siesta Hooded 20 Sleeping Bag | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F245457%2Frei-co-op-siesta-hooded-20-sleeping-bag, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F245457%2Frei-co-op-siesta-hooded-20-sleeping-bag]\n[Product: Rumpl Original Puffy Blanket | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F237298%2Frumpl-original-puffy-blanket, https://rumpl.sjv.io/c/482924/1237665/15234?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rumpl.com%2Fproducts%2Foriginal-puffy-blanket-seascape-ridge-mountains%3Fvariant%3D52746116858219, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F237298%2Frumpl-original-puffy-blanket]\n* Osprey’s Atmos AG 65 Pack is on sale in several colors and size configurations for around $258.93 ($112 off) at REI, which is one of the lowest prices we’ve seen. The 65-liter pack — which remains a go-to option for The Verge’s own Brandon Widder — is loaded with all sorts of bells and whistles, including an integrated rain cover, a floating top lid, and plenty of compression straps. The hallmark, though, is the ventilation system, which leverages a 3D-suspended mesh for comfort and breathability, making it a great pick for multi-day trips.\n* REI’s Ruckpack Waist Pack is on sale for $33.69 ($12 off) at REI, which is one of the best prices we’ve seen as of late. Made from a water-repellent material, this small adjustable bag can be worn around your waist or across your body and features three interior pockets for keeping your essentials organized.\n[Product: Sea to Summit Hanging Toiletry Bag | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F218322%2Fsea-to-summit-hanging-toiletry-bag-small]\n* The JetBoil Stash Cooking System is a compact, lightweight cooking system that’s currently down to $123.69 (about $41 off) at REI, which is one of the lowest prices we’ve seen all year. It features a standalone stove with a titanium burner and a 0.8-liter cooking pot, allowing you to boil water or heat food at your campsite. The pot comes with a lid and a pour handle, too, and everything can be stowed inside the pot when you’re finished, making it exceptionally easy to pack up.\n[Product: Sea to Summit Aeros Premium Pillow | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC04276%2Fsea-to-summit-aeros-premium-pillow%3Fcolor%3DPICANTE, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC04276%2Fsea-to-summit-aeros-premium-pillow%3Fcolor%3DPICANTE, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2FC04276%2Fsea-to-summit-aeros-premium-pillow%3Fcolor%3DPICANTE]\n* You can buy the ultralight Nemo Tensor in multiple sizes starting at REI for $131.93 (about $88 off). Designed for backpacking, the four-season sleeping pad offers 3.5 inches of cushioning and insulation to keep you warm in colder conditions, with a 5.4 R-value. The nylon construction is also relatively quiet, which, frankly, isn’t the case with many of the camping pads we’ve used over the years.\n* Nemo’s Stargaze Evo-X is on sale for $99.99 ($80 off) at REI, which is a great price for the surprisingly portable camping chair. The plush, versatile chair automatically reclines when you lean back, making it ideal for relaxing around the campsite (and stargazing). It also features a padded headrest, two cupholders, and a folding frame. And did we mention it swings? Because it swings.\n* REI’s Wonderland Cot is down to $187.39 ($62 off) at REI. The foldable cot — which is designed more for car camping than anything else — features a spacious, padded sleeping surface, an adjustable backrest, and a sturdy aluminum and steel frame that supports up to 300 pounds. The new version also comes with a webbing carrying strap, making it easier to lug around than prior models.\n[Product: Mpowerd Luci Solar String Lights: Color | https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F227376%2Fmpowerd-luci-solar-string-lights-18%2F]\n* Black Diamond’s Spot, the newer version of the Spot 400 headlamp, is on sale for $47.89 ($12 off) at REI. It offers up to 450 lumens of adjustable brightness, up from 400, along with red night vision and an IPX7 water-resistance rating. You can also choose to power it with standard AAA batteries or Black Diamond’s rechargeable battery.\n* The Petzl Tikka is on sale at REI for $18.77 (about $16 off). The basic headlamp is a great option that features a max output of 350 lumens, tilt functionality, and an IPX4 rating, making it safe to use in light rain. It also features a lock function that prevents it from accidentally turning on when packed.\n[Product: Black Diamond Moji Plus Lantern | https://www.amazon.com/BLACK-DIAMOND-Multi-colored-Rainproof-Backpacking/dp/B09NQL39X5/?tag=theverge02-20, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F202757%2Fblack-diamond-moji-lantern]\n* The Nite Ize Radiant 314 — which is currently down to $23.77 (about $22 off) at REI — provides 314 lumens of brightness, an impact-resistant design, and an IPX4 rating for water resistance. The rechargeable lantern can also last up to 96 hours on a single charge, while the built-in power bank can provide an extra boost of power to your phone in a pinch.\n* Luminaid’s Max 2-in-1 Power Lantern, which now inflates with a simple twist, is available for $47.19 (about $13 off) at REI. The nifty lantern delivers up to 200 lumens of light and lasts up to 50 hours; it also doubles as a portable phone charger, recharges either via solar power or USB, and folds flat.",
