      "summary": "Black Friday promises huge savings, but are the deals really as good as they seem?",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live          Use BBC.com or the new BBC App to listen to BBC podcasts, Radio 4 and the World Service outside the UK.Find out how to listen to other BBC stationsEpisode detailsRadio Ulster,·14 Nov 2026,·56 minsAvailable for 25 daysBlack Friday promises huge savings, but are the deals really as good as they seem? Before you click 'buy' Linzi Lima discusses the misleading discounts and marketing tactics that could leave shoppers paying more than they bargained for.\nLuxury serums, miracle ingredients and skincare routines costing hundreds of pounds. But when it comes to healthy skin, does a bigger price tag really mean better results? We separate the science from the hype...\nWhy do some products just not last like they used to? Like trainers that fall apart after a few wears - many consumers feel quality is slipping. As trusted heritage brands change hands and manufacturing is outsourced, we investigate what's driving the decline and hear from the founder of the website 'Worse on Purpose' about the growing problem.\nWould you rather stream your music or own it? In an age of playlists and subscriptions, more people are returning to vinyl records, CDs and other physical formats. We'll explore what's behind the revival and why music fans are once again choosing something they can hold in their hands.\nComplaints about parcel deliveries are on the rise, and now Ofcom is warning companies to raise their game or face tighter regulation. We hear from James Stinson of Ofcom in Belfast.\nAnd if you've got a consumer issue, a story to share, or a question you'd like us to investigate, get in touch: cfb@bbc.co.ukProgramme WebsiteMore episodes",
