    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-14-nvidia-allegedly-engineered-scarcity-by-funding-ai-startups-",
      "title": "Nvidia allegedly engineered scarcity by funding AI startups to buy its GPUs",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.techpowerup.com/354814/nvidia-allegedly-engineered-scarcity-by-funding-ai-startups-to-buy-its-gpus\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50493251\nPoints: 696\n# Comments: 403",
      "body": "Following the departure of now-former NVIDIA CEO, Jensen Huang, a new report by The Wall Street Journal (via Wccftech) has emerged alleging that NVIDIA artificially inflated the ongoing GPU and memory shortage by investing in AI startups that would go on to buy NVIDIA GPUs and build data centers. The reason behind this was to maintain the perception of ongoing high demand and to move an oversupply of semiconductors from TSMC.\nThe WSJ report cites an August meeting between Huang and his senior finance team, including NVIDIA's CFO and acting CEO, Colette Kress, during which Kress pushed for a reduction in circular financing agreements, in response to which Huang allegedly lay into Kress, calling her a \"deer in the headlights,\" after she had pushed to scale back NVIDIA's $250 billion deal with OpenAI. Jensen's push for further investment into small-scale cloud providers was seemingly in response to the changing tide that saw AI hyperscalers move away from off-the-shelf components in favor of custom solutions. The situation described in the report saw NVIDIA on the hook for an \"avalanche\" of GPUs from TSMC, for which it would have no immediate buyers. Part of the issue highlighted by Kress was also that these small-scale cloud providers NVIDIA was investing in could not afford to buy NVIDIA GPUs, meaning they, too, could be a financial dead end.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "speckx",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-14T02:52:59.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://www.techpowerup.com/img/ooCln2q3jkKNGHen.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.techpowerup.com/354814/nvidia-allegedly-engineered-scarcity-by-funding-ai-startups-to-buy-its-gpus",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-14-ggml-v1-0-0",
      "title": "Ggml v1.0.0",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml/releases/tag/v1.0.0\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50493062\nPoints: 300\n# Comments: 47",
      "body": "ggml 1.0.0 prunes the deprecated public API and the legacy DIAG_MASK ops, adds configurable YaRN truncation and FP8 support, and brings broad performance work across backends: few-row quantized matmuls and MoE fusion on CUDA/Metal, a Vulkan prefill FlashAttention path, a device-side MoE scheduler on SYCL, decomposed Adreno FlashAttention in OpenCL, new WebGPU kernels, expanded Hexagon op coverage, and scheduler improvements that avoid uploading unused inputs.\nPruned deprecated API and removed the legacy DIAG_MASK_INF/DIAG_MASK_ZERO ops, bumping the RPC protocol to reject incompatible peers (llama/29801, llama/31946)\nAdded ggml_rope_set_truncate/ggml_rope_get_truncate to control YaRN correction-bound rounding (llama/30206, llama/30802)\nImplemented the backward pass for TRI (llama/30712)\nAdded MUL_MAT src1 precision tests and gating for ggml_prec_set_acc (llama/31896, llama/31851)\nBumped the RPC protocol to v9 with faster loading and graceful failure on unreachable endpoints or failed handshakes (llama/29413, llama/30415)\nScheduler skips uploading inputs that are not read and prefetches only inputs produced by earlier splits (llama/31419, llama/32100)\nMoE cache can compute a share of the cache misses on the CPU and copy the results back asynchronously (llama/30966)\nMeta backend raises the compute view limit for buffers with few tensors (llama/31447)\nAdded few-row MMQ for batch sizes 2-24 and MMVF for BF16 few-row matmuls (llama/31533, llama/31959)\nAdded OCP FP8 support and fused NVFP4 gate/up matmuls with GLU in MMQ (llama/28413, llama/31296)\nExtended FlashAttention with an sm70 head-size-256 config and MMA head sizes 40/72 (llama/27997, llama/30285)\nImproved graph handling: skip compat checks on reuse, re-instantiate on cluster-dim changes, move graph state (llama/32004, llama/31284, llama/32001)\nMoE: skip empty MMQ stream-k tiles, linearize the MoE layout, and sanitize post-bias NaNs (llama/32067, llama/31047, llama/31005)\nAdded a debug buffer pool and halved the VMM pool reservation with reserve retries (llama/31919, llama/30542)\nHIP: use a fixed BLAS workspace and add an MFMA lightning indexer for CDNA2 (llama/31838, llama/29050)\nAdded a d_state=64 SSM_SCAN fast path and made radix Top-K deterministic for ties (llama/31818, llama/31084)\nFused MoE routing and kept fusable node groups inside a single command buffer (llama/31615, llama/31688)\nMade radix Top-K deterministic for ties, added mul_mm for 32<=K<64, and switched TRI to select (llama/31084, llama/30982, llama/30711)\nFixed GROUP_NORM for ne03>1 and out-of-bounds accesses in the FA output and SOLVE_TRI kernels (llama/31852, llama/31662, llama/32103)\nAdded an Intel FlashAttention prefill kernel (llama/29357)\nAdded batched tensor copies, a test-fusion interface, and ReBAR detection (llama/31418, llama/30769, llama/31658)\nEnabled dequantized KV with CM2, YaRN truncation, RDNA3/4 large-tile split-K, and large coopmat matmul on newer AMD drivers (llama/31526, llama/30802, llama/30280, llama/31587)\nAdded a tiled-transpose concat shader and FWHT kernels for block widths above 512 (llama/30591, llama/29772)\nFixed MoltenVK out-of-bounds accesses, GROUP_NORM workgroup limits, and FA scratch sizing (llama/31890, llama/31930, llama/30487)\nCapped scalar FlashAttention at 8 rows for large heads on Qualcomm (llama/30829)\nAdded a device-side MoE scheduler (llama/30156)\nMade the oneDNN FA cache thread-safe and un-gated fused SDPA for Alchemist at head_dim=64 (llama/31138, llama/31574)\nCached the device id and reject buffers that would exceed VRAM (llama/31126, llama/32013, llama/31285)\nAdded exact rounding for CPY to Q4_1/Q5_1/Q8_0, strided CLAMP, and f16 SWIGLU_OAI (llama/31465, llama/31784, llama/30857)\nFixed AOT for allocations above 4GB (llama/31873)\nAdded decomposed Adreno FlashAttention and improved decode performance (llama/32046, llama/31633)\nAdded q6_k tiled, q8_0, and f32/q5_k multi-column GEMV kernels and f32 MUL_MAT_ID (llama/31758, llama/30947, llama/31783)\nAdded arange, non-contiguous sigmoid, repeat for f16/i32/i16/bf16, and DSV4 HC pre/post kernels (llama/31829, llama/31687, llama/31782, llama/31623)\nEnabled multi-column GEMV by default for Adreno X2 (llama/31694)\nAdded batched tensor API support and returned maxBufferSize from get_max_size (llama/31473, llama/31348)\nAdded GROUP_NORM, MEAN, COUNT_EQUAL, and PAD_REFLECT_1D kernels (llama/31490, llama/31591, llama/31578, llama/31877)\nSupported the YaRN truncation config (llama/30802)\nAdded Q5_0/Q5_1 support and optimized conv_2d while adding conv_3d (llama/32094, llama/31814)\nFused post-norm residual add into RMS_NORM_MUL and added set_tensor_n (llama/31822, llama/31744)\nAdded automatic libhtp loading and fixed 64-bit FastRPC handle truncation (llama/31781, llama/30952)\nFixed the host build with clang-cl on Windows ARM64 (llama/32011)\nSwitched MUL_MAT to F32 src1 and accumulate FlashAttention V in F32 (llama/31854, llama/29810)\nAdded SpacemiT GATED_DELTA_NET RVV and Q4_1 32x256 HP kernels and enabled IME2 MXFP4 repack (llama/31897, llama/31929, llama/31776)\nEnabled the 4x4 simd_gemm tile on ARM NEON and added bf16/q8_0 VXE to llamafile (llama/32128, llama/31866)\nFail early when a buffer type is unsupported (llama/31270)\nAccept non-zdnn tensors, invalidate compute tensors after each op, and fix release backend lib detection (llama/31824, llama/31905)\nSupported the YaRN truncation config (llama/30802)\nReleases and versioning of ggml-org projects\n417a024 ggml : bump version to 1.0.0 (#1690)\n771b3d9 requirements : fix numpy for python 3.14 (#1691)\nec04faf fix(hexagon): make host build work with clang-cl on Windows ARM64 (llama/32011)\nb45738e examples : adapt to removal of ggml_diag_mask_inf\n5f29555 ggml : prune (llama/29801)\n076861c hexagon: add Q5_0 and Q5_1 support (llama/32094)\n63ec52d Title: CUDA: few-row MMQ for BS 2-24 (llama/31533)\nc6fe796 ggml : route GATED_DELTA_NET to the SpacemiT RVV kernel (llama/31897)\n4ae6e72 vulkan : Intel FA kernel for prefill. (llama/29357)\nb22071c ggml-cpu: use the 4x4 simd_gemm tile on ARM NEON (llama/32128)\nba8b013 CUDA: Optimize prefil via fuse of w_s scale in epilogue MMQ for nvfp4 checkpoints (llama/26048)\n05f605a ggml-backend : prefetch only inputs computed by earlier splits (llama/32100)\nb8a5b87 ggml : dispatch SpacemiT Q4_1 32x256 through the HP kernel (llama/31929)\n7a8cef5 sycl: make oneDNN FA cache thread-safe and memoize runtime failures (llama/31138)\n6dfea1a sycl : fix AOT for more than 4GB (llama/31873)\n012ff44 sycl : use cached device-id in set_main_device (llama/32013)\n2f9d47b CUDA: add cuda debug buffer pool (llama/31919)\n522d257 opencl: add bin kernel kernel_gemm_noshuffle_q4_0_f32_32b_trans_ila_a7_bin (llama/30947)\n0f9dcb7 CUDA: skip empty MoE tiles in MMQ stream-k fixup (llama/32067)\n6bed9a8 opencl: add decomposed FA for Adreno (llama/32046)\na357e7b metal : prevent out-of-bounds reads in SOLVE_TRI kernel (llama/32103)\nc36ccd8 vulkan: support batched tensor copy API (llama/31418)\n1bffc59 backend : re-instantiate CUDA graphs when the cluster dims of a kernel change (llama/31284)\n8153155 ROCm/HIP: fixed BLAS workspace instead of rocBLAS allocating one per call (llama/31838)\nad7d200 cpu: accumulate flash attention V in F32 (llama/29810)\n7f4a2db webgpu: add PAD_REFLECT_1D support (llama/31877)\n0f51454 vulkan: allow dequantized KV optimization with CM2 (llama/31526)\neb4de49 vulkan: allocate the device fault vendor binary buffer (llama/32008)\n6b7f47a cuda : use MMVF for BF16 matrices of few rows at small batch sizes (llama/31959)\n77d01f1 cuda : add sm70 FlashAttention config case for DKQ=256, DV=256, ncols=64 (llama/27997)\nbd37ba0 cuda : fattn mma head sizes 40 72 (llama/30285)\n161ca15 CUDA: Add OCP FP8 support (llama/28413)\n06faf80 sycl : fixed sycl CLAMP to actually support strided view (llama/31784)\na986181 cuda : remove unused ids and type_src0 parameters (llama/32018)\n55104b2 llama : Add FP8 KV-cache support (llama/28392)\n0753641 ggml : add MUL_MAT src1 precision tests and gating (llama/31896)\n1cd16bd cuda : remove unused quantize_cuda_t typedef (llama/31884)\n4a18cdd cuda : halve VMM pool reservation size and retry on cuMemAddressReserve failure (llama/30542)\n1c9ac9d CUDA: skip graph compat check when graph is being reused (llama/32004)\n999c725 ggml : fix FreeBSD Vulkan build by setting _XOPEN_SOURCE=700 (llama/31701)\n47bc1d8 CUDA: move graph and concurrent stream state out of common.cuh (llama/32001)\ndf70e12 cann: fail early when checking if buffer type is supported (llama/31270)\ne447eb5 sycl: Add device-side MoE scheduler (llama/30156)\n9a1c582 vulkan: add tiled-transpose concat shader for Qwen models (llama/30591)\n8b3c8cf ggml-rpc : fail gracefully on unreachable endpoints and failed handshakes (llama/30415)\nf860f1d vulkan: Divide GROUP_NORM workgroup to 2D to avoid maxComputeWorkGroupCount limit (llama/31930)\neb5571a vulkan: Fix out of bounds reads/writes on MoltenVK (llama/31890)\n5a9a264 vulkan: cap scalar flash attention at 8 rows for large heads on Qualcomm (llama/30829)\n5610f41 sycl: un-gate oneDNN fused SDPA for Alchemist at head_dim=64 (llama/31574)\n487cadf hexagon: fix 64-bit FastRPC handle truncation on close (llama/30952)\nbe37c9c ggml-zdnn: accept non-zdnn tensors, invalidate compute tensors after every op (llama/31824)\n294d5fc ggml : implement the backward pass for TRI (llama/30712)\ne18c2c6 ggml-backend: don't upload inputs that are not read (llama/31419)\ne84d36b metal : prevent out-of-bounds writes to the Metal FA output buffer (llama/31662)\n0dd184f metal : make ggml_tri select instead of scaling by the comparison (llama/30711)\nb6d482c opencl : include climits (llama/31935)\n62de780 RPC: Improve loading times (llama/29413)\na7276d0 ggml : support YaRN truncation config on openvino, sycl, vulkan, webgpu, rpc (llama/30802)\nda89459 sycl: cache device-id (llama/31126)\nfb57085 tests: bound the test_rope tolerance by the f32 angle resolution (llama/31874)\ne43d847 opencl: add f32 MUL_MAT_ID (llama/31783)\nd1c1e4b ggml-zdnn: fix release binary not detecting backend lib (llama/31905)\n7e7b6e9 mtmd: refactoring: remove clip.h, consolidate code into mtmd (llama/31865)\n5a0e536 cpu: enable SpacemiT IME2 MXFP4 dense repack (llama/31776)\n7f4b25f llamafile: impl bf16 and q8_0 vxe (llama/31866)\nf22fc6a ggml : update CUDA/Metal radix Top-K to make tied selections deterministic (llama/31084)\n47b8b4f ggml-cuda : add d_state=64 fast path to SSM_SCAN kernel (llama/31818)\nb524960 webgpu : add COUNT_EQUAL support (llama/31578)\n75a4f5a ggml : switch to F32 src1 in the CPU backend (llama/31854)\n6cddab2 llama, mtmd: follow the reference precision of ggml_prec_set_acc calls (llama/31851)\n7353275 opencl: improve q8_0 and MoE small-n verification for spec (llama/31831)\n8f1404e hexagon: support for automatic loading of libhtp without legacy env vars (llama/31781)\n91c102a sycl: exact rounding in CPY to Q4_1, Q5_1 and Q8_0 (llama/31465)\n8cf32bc sycl: refuse device buffers that would exceed VRAM (llama/31285)\nd969b07 hexagon: n_hvx and n_threads cleanup (llama/31857)\n5746ebd llama_moe_cache: run missed experts on CPU, add tuning script (llama/30966)\na49f174 sycl: add f16 support for SWIGLU_OAI (llama/30857)\nc6a0780 metal : fix GROUP_NORM for ne03 > 1 and non-contiguous inputs (llama/31852)\n1e5c3e0 webgpu : Implement group norm kernel (llama/31490)\n37ecdca vulkan: Add 'readonly' to decodeBuf declarations. (llama/31833)\nc08538b CUDA: fix shared memory bank conflicts in the lightning indexer (llama/31803)\n07b8362 opencl: add arange (llama/31829)\nf55a504 meta : raise the compute view limit for buffers with few tensors (llama/31447)\n2870133 hexagon: fuse post-norm residual add into RMS_NORM_MUL (llama/31822)\na135ec6 hexagon: conv_2d optimizations and support for conv_3d (llama/31814)\ne3d3633 tests : qualify isnan and signbit with std:: (llama/31791)\na7d3330 tests : override hardware_concurrency in CI (llama/31797)\nab7ca9c opencl: support repeat for f16, i32, i16, bf16 (llama/31782)\n9290392 webgpu: add batched tensor API (get_tensor_n and set_tensor_n) (llama/31473)\nf594fed vulkan: detect ReBAR support, avoid BAR allocations if unavailable (llama/31658)\n38e4be2 CUDA: fix Maxwell build (llama/31787)\n8bd6b61 opencl: add q6_k multi column tiled GEMV for speculative verification and refactoring (llama/31758)\nd3ce63d hexagon: Implement set_tensor_n and improve repacking/tiling robustness (llama/31744)\n9b1880f ggml-cuda: sanitize post-bias NaNs in MoE selection (llama/31005)\n7e607b8 vulkan: Implement test-fusion interface (llama/30769)\n2188d13 CUDA: use highest compiled arch in get_mmvq_mmid_max_batch (llama/31679)\n114ce5e vulkan: RDNA3/4 Large-Tile Split-K Optimization (llama/30280)\ne074347 metal : fuse DeepSeek-V4/V4.1 and GLM MoE routing (llama/31615)\nf0f5b42 CUDA/HIP: matrix-core (MFMA) lightning indexer for CDNA2 (gfx90a) (llama/29050)\nfa8c617 CUDA: linearize MoE data layout for MMQ/MMF (llama/31047)\n1690d2e vulkan: FWHT kernels for block widths above 512 (llama/29772)\n40278c4 vulkan : check combined K+V f16 scratch size in FA dequant path (llama/30487)\n25b845e ggml : support truncate=false for YaRN (llama/30206)\nb2ce926 metal : use mul_mm for 32 <= K < 64 (llama/30982)\n1a5f477 webgpu : add MEAN support (llama/31591)\n2ab6d6c vulkan: Re-enable large coopmat matmul configuration on AMD proprietary driver 26.10.1+ (llama/31587)\n19df6cf tests: fix CI flakes of TOPK_MOE caused by near ties (llama/31426)\na0df99d metal: keep fusable node groups inside one command buffer (llama/31688)\n3a996db opencl: enable f32 and q5_k multi column GEMV by default for Adreno X2 (llama/31694)\nd75184e opencl: support non-contig sigmoid (llama/31687)\nc634501 opencl: add DSV4_HC_PRE and DSV4_HC_POST (llama/31623)\n0816137 Title: CUDA: fuse NVFP4 gate/up matmuls and GLU in MMQ (llama/31296)\n4ac0dae opencl: improve decode perf with FA (llama/31633)\n4f681f2 webgpu: return maxBufferSize from get_max_size and avoid whole-buffer bindings in memset/clear (llama/31348)\ncd6d2b7 docs : sync ggml_type enum in gguf.md (#1685)",
