      "id": "hackernews-2026-11-14-amtrak-booking-system-experiencing-major-issues-amid-nationw",
      "title": "Amtrak booking system experiencing major issues amid nationwide FAA ground stop",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.fox5dc.com/news/amtrak-outage-ticket-booking-faa-ground-stop-november-13-2026\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50492315\nPoints: 171\n# Comments: 60",
      "body": "Amtrak said its booking system is returning to normal after a network outage that coincided with a nationwide FAA ground stop.Users on social media started sharing frustrations over ticket reservations Friday afternoon, with travelers showing error messages on Amtrak&apos;s website and app.Hundreds of users reported issues on DownDetector, beginning shortly before 5 p.m. Friday, with another surge just before 6 p.m.In response to a request for comment, Amtrak&apos;s Communications Director W. Kyle Anderson said that &quot;Amtrak service is operating normally, and we are seeing increased demand for travel across our network.&quot;Responding to a frustrated customer Friday, Amtrak officials said in a post on X that the booking issues were related to a system-wide update, but did not elaborate.Around 9 p.m. officials said the booking systems were returning to normal.&#xA0;The company said some customers may still experience issues while processing payments, booking trips or modifying existing reservations. Amtrak&#x2019;s call centers experienced higher-than-normal call volumes, resulting in longer wait times for some.FOX 5 DC attempted to call the support number during the outage, around 8 p.m., but an automated message said officials were unable to take calls due to &quot;unusually high call volume.&quot;The outage came as thousands of travelers across the country scrambled for new plans, after the Federal Aviation Administration issued a nationwide ground stop &#x2014; the first since January 2023 and just the second since the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks.The FAA has said that the ground stop was ordered due to a &quot;temporary telecommunications outage.&quot; It has since been lifted.&#xA0;",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "transportation",
        "travel"
      ],
      "author": "snow_mac",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-14T00:52:29.000Z",
