    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-13-driver-who-fled-to-latvia-after-killing-schoolboy-jailed",
      "title": "Driver who fled to Latvia after killing schoolboy jailed",
      "summary": "Aleksanders Dolars is brought to justice after fleeing the UK when he hit Keaton Slater at 70mph.",
      "body": "A speeding driver who fled to Latvia after killing a 12-year-old boy when he hit him at more than 70mph has been jailed. Aleksanders Dolars evaded capture for Keaton Slater's death for more than two years because there was no extradition treaty between Latvia and the UK post-Brexit.He was finally brought to justice in August this year following a determined campaign by Keaton's parents, when he was flown to England to appear at Warwick Crown Court.Dolars, 23, was sentenced to nine years and four months by Judge Kristina Montgomery KC who told him: \"Your selfish and dangerous driving took his life.\" Keaton's family said the sentence was not long enough.The court heard Dolars had been driving at 75-76mph in a 30mph zone when he struck the schoolboy in Coventry, killing him instantly.Keaton, a devoted Coventry City fan, was travelling home from school with friends on 14 June, 2024, and had just got off a bus.He had stepped out onto Radford Road and prepared to cross but the court heard he would not have seen Dolars' BMW at that time.As it approached him he attempted to run out of its way with no success.Dolars, who bowed his head throughout the hearing, did not stop and fled to his native Latvia within days.The hearing also heard statements from Keaton's brothers, Kai and Josh.\"Losing Keaton has left a space in my heart that can never be filled,\" Kai said. \"Keaton's death didn't just take away my little brother - I'll never get to see the man he would be.\"Knowing that someone could leave the scene after what happened, I will never understand.\"Josh, Keaton's half brother, said he \"struggled to comprehend\" what happened and was angry Keaton had been taken away.\"The defendant has left a trail of destruction that cannot be repaired and will be with us forever,\" he said.Owatemi sat in court with the family, and speaking after the sentencing, she said: \"Today has been the most heartbreaking day I have experienced as a Member of Parliament.\"She added: \"As a mother, I cannot begin to imagine receiving the phone call that tells you your child is never coming home. \"I cannot imagine the pain of losing your son so suddenly, knowing that his life has been taken because of someone else's actions.\"She also said she was \"incredibly angry\" at the sentence handed down.\"I do not believe this sentence reflects the seriousness of what happened to Keaton, or the suffering his loved ones have been forced to endure,\" she said.Owatemi said she struggled to understand how Keaton's parents \"are expected to accept this as justice\".She said she would support the family in an attempt to get the sentence reviewed by the Court of Appeal.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T20:53:14.000Z",
