    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-11-13-chatgpt-wallet-lets-openai-s-dots-agents-make-purchases-for-",
      "title": "ChatGPT Wallet lets OpenAI’s Dots agents make purchases for you",
      "summary": "After launching its Dots AI agents platform earlier this year, OpenAI is launching a wallet for the agents. ChatGPT Wallet is rolling out starting today for ChatGPT Pro subscribers in the US aged 18 and older using a US billing address and \"eligible US-issued American Express, Chase, Mastercard and Visa cards.\"\nAfter adding a card to the wallet, your Dots agents can use it to buy things in respons",
      "body": "After launching its Dots AI agents platform earlier this year, OpenAI is launching a wallet for the agents. ChatGPT Wallet is rolling out starting today for ChatGPT Pro subscribers in the US aged 18 and older using a US billing address and “eligible US-issued American Express, Chase, Mastercard and Visa cards.”\nAfter adding a card to the wallet, your Dots agents can use it to buy things in response to your prompts, but they’ll check in with you each time before checking out. OpenAI’s support page says every purchase with ChatGPT Wallet requires a security check with biometric verification like Face ID or a fingerprint scan.\n[Image: Users have to approve every purchase from ChatGPT Wallet. https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/openai-chatgpt-wallet-approval-pop-up.jpeg?quality=90&strip=all]\nAfter you review the AI agent’s purchase and sign off on it, OpenAI says that, similar to using tap to pay, Apple Pay, or Google Wallet, it substitutes your credit card details with a payment token, so your actual card info isn’t shared with your Dots agent or the business you’re buying from. Eventually, OpenAI says it expects “users to be able to delegate purchases entirely to their agent by setting clear parameters—such as spending limits, purchase categories, or time periods—and pre-approve those purchases.”\nChatGPT Wallet might not work everywhere. Some retailers have restrictions on AI agents or block them altogether. Earlier this year, Amazon blocked Meta’s Muse agents. OpenAI says that in order for agents to use ChatGPT Wallet, “websites need to ensure agents are not inadvertently blocked, and payment and risk systems need to recognize legitimate purchases made by agents.”",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "AI",
        "News",
        "OpenAI",
        "Tech"
      ],
      "author": "Stevie Bonifield",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T20:45:10.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/10/STKS539_AI_AGENTS_SHOPPING_B.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.732984293194,100,78.534031413613",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1033425/openai-chatgpt-wallet",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-11-13-cmf-s-milk-carton-shaped-bluetooth-speaker-is-down-to-a-new-",
      "title": "CMF’s milk carton-shaped Bluetooth speaker is down to a new low price",
      "summary": "The CMF Speaker S comes in four colors: white, dark gray, orange, and turquoise. | Image: CMF by Nothing\t\n\nBluetooth speakers are often boring boxes in plain colors, but not this one! As part of Nothing’s ongoing early Black Friday promo, you can grab its unique, milk carton-shaped CMF Speaker S from Amazon and Nothing for just $39. That’s a solid $20 discount and the lowest price we’ve seen on No",
      "body": "Bluetooth speakers are often boring boxes in plain colors, but not this one! As part of Nothing’s ongoing early Black Friday promo, you can grab its unique, milk carton-shaped CMF Speaker S from Amazon and Nothing for just $39. That’s a solid $20 discount and the lowest price we’ve seen on Nothing’s newfangled wireless speaker, which hit the market about a month ago.\n[Product: CMF by Nothing Speaker S | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HDYM4KS3?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=87443X1797501&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.nothing.tech%2Fproducts%2Fcmf-speaker-s]\nThe CMF Speaker S is the smaller of the two recently-released models — the larger Series M is also on sale at Amazon for $79 ($30 off) — and sports a 45mm driver with two passive radiators to help with low-end frequencies. It can run for up to 18 hours on a single charge and carries an IP68 rating for water and dust resistance. Despite its carefree aesthetic, it also supports stereo pairing with a second Seris S speaker, Bluetooth 6, fast pairing via multiple methods (including NFC and Google Fast Pair), and audio over USB-C.\nIn addition to their great sound and compact footprint, both the Speaker S and Speaker M feature removable faceplates and multifunction front knobs. Not only can you swap them out to customize the colors, but CMF plans to share STL files so anyone with a 3D printer can create their own attachments and looks.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Black Friday",
