      "id": "bbc-2026-11-13-rosal-a-scoops-historic-third-best-album-award-at-latin-gram",
      "title": "Rosalía scoops historic third best album award at Latin Grammys",
      "summary": "The Spanish singer is recognised for her fourth album Lux which was released last year to rave reviews.",
      "body": "Image source, Getty ImagesImage caption, Rosalía released her fourth album Lux last year to rave reviews ByRiyah CollinsBBC NewsbeatSpanish star Rosalía has made history as the first woman to win the best album award at the Latin Grammys three times, after being recognised for her project Lux. The singer took home five trophies in total, including two for her track La Perla which was named song of the year and best pop song.La Perla was also nominated for record of the year but missed out to Argentine singer Milo J's song Niño.Rosalía released Lux last year to rave reviews and collecting her award at the ceremony in Las Vegas on Thursday, she said: \"To all the people who told me I wasn't good enough, or that my music was too weird, I'm thankful I didn't listen.\"The Barcelona-born artist then added: \"Now I'm winning these prizes.\"Rosalía, who opened the ceremony with a performance of some of her biggest songs, was honoured with the prize for best alternative music album.She also picked up best shortform music video for her track Sauvignon Blanc. The singer had previously won best album for El Mal Querer in 2019 and Motomami in 2022 - and her third Lux is also tipped to be a favourite when nominations are announced for the Grammys next week.Image source, Getty ImagesImage caption, After a career spanning three decades, Daddy Yankee was recognised with a lifetime achievement awardIt was also a big night for Puerto Rican reggaeton legend Daddy Yankee, who won the person of the year award.He performed some of his best-loved tracks including Gasolina and Con Calma, and was joined on stage by rappers including LL Cool J and French Montana.Punjabi singer Diljit Dosanjh, who collabed with Daddy Yankee on Pokito, even took a break from his Aura India tour for the set, making him the first Indian artist to perform at the Latin Grammys.Dosanjh superfan Divanshi Arora described the singer's appearance as \"a cultural revolution\".\"It's really invigorating and motivating to see someone from my country has made it all around the world,\" she tells Newsbeat.She sees a lot of similarities between South American and Punjabi communities and hopes this leads to more collaborations - with a link-up between Dosanjh and Bad Bunny top of her wishlist.Daddy Yankee was presented with the lifetime achievement award by Janet Jackson, who told him in Spanish that his music \"has inspired an entire generation\".Image source, Getty ImagesImage caption, Diljit Dosanjh became the first Indian artist to perform at the Latin GrammysAccepting the prize for record of the year, Milo J seemed surprised to have won ahead of strong competition from Karol G, Jorge Drexler, Carin León as well as Rosalía.The 20-year-old took home four trophies in the end and gave a shout out to Argentine folk music.He described Niño as the song \"I'm most proud of out of everything I've created so far\".\"Long live Argentine folk music,\" he added.Elsewhere, ARIA VEGA was named best new artist and songwriter of the year went to Sara Schell.Additional reporting by Abu Bakar YasinListen to Newsbeat live at 12:45 and 17:45 weekdays - or listen back here.More on this story",
      "source": "BBC",
