      "title": "Jensen Huang was having a third affair, Reuters reports",
      "summary": "Reuters is withholding the name of the new employee linked to Huang, but says she is an employee of Nvidia.",
      "body": "Nvidia founder Jensen Huang was having a separate affair with an employee that has not been previously reported, Reuters reported on Thursday.\nHuang stepped down as CEO and board member for the company earlier today, in the wake of news of extramarital affairs with accused spy Alice Huang and Nvidia VP of Healthcare Kimberly Powell. CFO Colette Kress has stepped in as interim CEO, but no permanent successor has been named.\nReuters is withholding the name of the new employee linked to Huang but says she is an employee of Nvidia.\nHuang has been called before Congress to testify about the national security implications of his relationship with Alice Huang in the coming weeks — but it’s unclear how much more will be revealed before the hearings take place. Already, his abrupt fall from grace is expected to have significant repercussions for the industry at large.",
