      "id": "bbc-2026-11-12-who-is-nvidia-s-interim-ceo-colette-kress-and-who-could-take",
      "title": "Who is Nvidia's interim CEO Colette Kress - and who could take over permanently?",
      "summary": "Chief financial officer Colette Kress in in charge of Nvidia for now, but several others are in the frame as potential successors.",
      "body": "Image source, Bloomberg via Getty Images/ReutersImage caption, Arm's boss Rene Haas (L), Nvidia's Colette Kress (C) and Chris Malachowsky (R) have been named as possible successors ByOsmond ChiaBusiness reporterNvidia is now facing a scenario few would have considered until very recently - a future without Jensen Huang.The influential co-founder of the AI chip-making giant resigned on Thursday over reports of extramarital affairs, one of which was with a woman suspected of being a Chinese spy.Chief financial officer Colette Kress is in charge, for now, as the tech giant faces one of its biggest challenges - finding the right person to permanently lead the business that Huang helped create more than three decades ago and turned into one of the world's most valuable companies.We take a look at which candidates have emerged as potential successors. The finance chief Image source, NvidiaImage caption, Colette Kress is chief financial officer at Nvidia Colette Kress has been an industry veteran for more than 30 years, having previously held high positions at tech firms like Cisco and Microsoft.Kress, who also serves as Nvidia's executive vice-president, has seen the firm's transformation from making chips for video games in the early 1990s to becoming an AI semiconductor powerhouse.She has \"fronted every earnings call\" alongside Huang and is a \"familiar and trusted voice for the market at a time when it badly needs one,\" said Josh Gilbert, an analyst at investment firm eToro.But doing the job permanently could be a different story, said Gilbert, as the firm, known for its edge in technology, could want an engineer in the chair.The co-founder and the engineerImage source, Getty ImagesImage caption, Chris Malachowsky is one of Nvidia's three co-founders Another option is Chris Malachowsky, who founded Nvidia alongside Huang and Curtis Priem, and is the only executive that shares the same level of seniority.Malachowsky has played a key part in developing the company's computing technology.Ian Buck, who oversees Nvidia's high-performance computing business, has also emerged as a potential candidate if the company is keen to put an engineer in the top job.Buck was among the early pioneers who helped popularise the use of graphic processors beyond gaming applications.\"He could protect Nvidia's technological edge, but his ability to manage the wider commercial relationships and geopolitical challenges would face scrutiny,\" said Charu Chanana, investment strategist at investment bank Saxo.  Today, Nvidia's leading processors are widely regarded as the gold standard for AI development.Huang's children also work at Nvidia in executive positions but are relatively young and inexperienced.Apple and Arm's top brassNvidia is likely to favour an internal appointment initially but could look externally for a more permanent replacement, said Jun Bei Liu, founder and lead portfolio manager at Ten Cap.Several names of tech entrepreneurs outside of Nvidia have been floated by experts. US President Donald Trump suggested Apple's former chief executive, Tim Cook, as a good replacement.\"NOW THAT Nvidia CEO JENSEN HUANG, who has done a fantastic job, has resigned, there is only one man to take his place - TIM COOK of Apple. A Legend replaces a Legend!\" he wrote on Truth Social.Liu said Cook could be a possible choice as someone familiar with managing global supply chains, though she questioned whether he would be willing to leave the iPhone maker, where he is the chair. Image source, ReutersImage caption, Apple's Tim Cook (R) with Jensen Huang (L) and his wife Lori Huang at the White HouseLiu and Chanana also suggested Rene Haas, chief executive of Arm Holdings, the UK chip designer.Nvidia's processors are made with the help of chipmakers around the world, including Taiwan's TSMC and South Korea's SK Hynix and Samsung.Image source, Getty ImagesImage caption, Rene Haas is the boss of Arm HoldingsHaas is familiar with leading a publicly-listed company and would bring semiconductor experience, though Nvidia's business model is considerably different from Arm's, said Chanana. \"The challenge is finding someone who can combine Jensen's technical understanding, strategic vision and relationships across the global technology industry,\" Liu said.What now for Nvidia?Ten Cap's Liu had believed it was just a matter of time before Huang would step down as Nvidia's chief executive.\"The issue is no longer simply about personal conduct,\" she said. \"It is about corporate governance, national security concerns and maintaining confidence in the leadership of one of the world's most strategically important companies.\"Several major investment firms have downgraded their forecasts for the chip giant - a rare shift given investors' longstanding optimism about the company.An early indication came as markets opened in New York shortly after Huang's resignation was announced. Nvidia shares opened down more than 13%, wiping more than half a trillion dollars off the firm's share market value.Image source, Bloomberg via Getty ImagesImage caption, Jensen Huang's departure leaves a void in the influential AI giantStacy Rasgon, senior analyst in US semiconductors at Bernstein Research, wrote in a note to investors that \"our gut tells us we probably haven't fully probed the depths of what might be found here\".Rasgon halved Bernstein's share price target for Nvidia and said: \"We've had enough and prefer to watch from the sidelines.\"Ray Wang, chief executive of Constellation Research, said the crisis isn't so much an issue for the wider AI industry but rather one for Nvidia itself which has to consider if the person it appoints as its chief executive has the same appeal as Huang.\"That's really what the issue is, because a lot of these partnerships and investments have been made because of the trust with with Jensen,\" he said.Additional reporting by Kali HaysMore on this story",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "business",
