      "title": "Jensen Huang resigning effective immediately",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.stocktitan.net/news/NVDA/nvidia-announces-ceo-03al5m45ne1p.html\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50467092\nPoints: 15\n# Comments: 14",
      "body": "The board expects operations, customer commitments and the product roadmap to continue without interruption.\nSentiment and the balance of pointsRhea-AI Sentiment reads the wording of the document, how positive or negative its language is on a 1 to 5 scale. The balance of points shown with the takes weighs what the document actually discloses, so the two can disagree, for example when a trial that missed its main goal is described in upbeat language.How Sentiment worksHow the balance works\nNVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) announced Jensen Huang’s immediate resignation as president, chief executive officer and board member, with Colette Kress appointed interim CEO.Kress will retain her executive vice president and chief financial officer roles until a permanent successor is named. The board is initiating a search that will consider internal and external candidates. Harvey C. Jones was appointed the board’s first-ever chair.NVIDIA will report third-quarter fiscal 2027 results on November 17 at approximately 1:20 p.m. PT, followed by its earnings call at 2 p.m. PT, as previously scheduled.\nMkt Cap at Last Price\nOn Nov 12, the day this news came out, the latest delayed price for NVDA is 10.38% below the previous close.\nOur momentum scanner has recorded 167 alerts for this stock so far that day.\nThe latest delayed price is $155.70.\nRelative volume is exceptionally heavy at 26.2x what this stock usually trades by this time of day.\nData tracked by StockTitan Argus (15 min delayed). Upgrade to Gold for real-time data.\nAI-generated analysis. How Rhea-AI works. Not financial advice.\nSee more from StockTitan in Google Search and AI answers.\nAdds StockTitan as a preferred source · opens Google\n11/12/2026 - 08:48 AM EST\nJensen Huang ResignsColette Kress, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer, Appointed Interim CEOHarvey C. Jones Appointed First-Ever Chair of the Board  SANTA CLARA, Calif., Nov.  12, 2026  (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) Board of Directors announced today that Jensen Huang has resigned as President, Chief Executive Officer, and a member of the Board, effective immediately.  Colette Kress, current Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of NVIDIA, has agreed to serve as Interim Chief Executive Officer. Kress will continue to serve as Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer while serving as Interim Chief Executive Officer until a permanent successor has been named. The Board is initiating a search for a permanent Chief Executive Officer and will consider internal and external candidates.  Kress has served as Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of NVIDIA since joining the company in September 2013. During her tenure, she has led the company’s finance organization and has played a key role in NVIDIA’s growth and evolution. Prior to joining NVIDIA, Kress spent nearly 25 years in finance roles at leading technology companies, including Cisco and Microsoft.  The Board of Directors appointed Harvey C. Jones as its first-ever Chair of the Board.  Mr. Jones has been an entrepreneur, technology executive, and active venture investor for over 30 years, including serving as Chief Executive Officer and Executive Chairman of Synopsys.  “Colette has helped lead NVIDIA through a period of extraordinary growth and has a deep understanding of our business, customers, operations and financial position,” said Harvey Jones, Chair of the NVIDIA Board of Directors. “She is supported by an experienced leadership team that has been instrumental in executing NVIDIA’s strategy and advancing its technology roadmap. The Board has full confidence in Colette and the leadership team, and we expect the company’s operations, customer commitments and product roadmap to continue without interruption.”    “NVIDIA’s strength has always come from its people, and together with our leadership team, I am committed to building on the extraordinary foundation Jensen created over the last 33 years,” said Colette Kress, Interim CEO and CFO, NVIDIA. “We will continue advancing the work that has made NVIDIA a leader in accelerated computing and AI, and execute on the opportunities ahead. Our focus remains on serving our customers, partners, developers and shareholders.”   Jensen’s contributions to NVIDIA are profound. NVIDIA is one of the most consequential technology companies in the world. The Board and the company thank Jensen for his immeasurable contributions to the company and the industry.  NVIDIA will report its third-quarter fiscal 2027 financial results on Tuesday, November 17, at approximately 1:20 p.m. PT, as previously scheduled, followed by its earnings call at 2 p.m. PT.   About NVIDIANVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) is the world leader in AI and accelerated computing.  © 2026 NVIDIA Corporation. All rights reserved. NVIDIA and the NVIDIA logo are trademarks and/or registered trademarks of NVIDIA Corporation in the U.S. and other countries.\nAI-generated questions and answers. How Rhea-AI works. Not financial advice.\nWho is replacing Jensen Huang as NVIDIA CEO?\nColette Kress has been appointed interim CEO following Jensen Huang’s immediate resignation. She will also remain executive vice president and chief financial officer until a permanent successor is named. The board is initiating a search considering internal and external candidates.",
