    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-11-12-resident-evil-requiem-sweeps-golden-joystick-awards",
      "title": "Resident Evil Requiem sweeps Golden Joystick Awards",
      "summary": "The latest instalment in the franchise, which is marking 30 years, bagged the top prize.",
      "body": "Resident Evil Requiem and its makers have won big at the Golden Joystick Awards, which celebrate the year's most popular games.Released in February, it was the latest instalment of the global survival horror phenomenon, which has also spawned books, films and TV programmes since it was first released 30 years ago.At Wednesday's awards ceremony, it scooped ultimate game of the year, console game of the year, best game trailer, and best lead performer for the game's star Angela Sant'Albano, who plays protagonist Grace Ashcroft. Meanwhile its makers, Japanese studio Capcom, was named studio of the year and was also recognised for other games, including Onimusha: Way of the Sword and Pragmata. FBI agent Grace Ashcroft was a brand new lead character in Resident Evil Requiem who, along with returning fan favourite Leon S. Kennedy, explores old haunts, such as Racoon City's police department as they investigate a series of mysterious deaths. Securing 17% of the public vote, it was named ultimate game of the year ahead of other contenders Phantom Blade Zero, Crimson Desert, Control Resonant and The Blood of Dawnwalker. Best Storytelling - Dispatch Best Audio Design - Onimusha: Way of the Sword Best Multiplayer Game - Meccha ChameleonBest Visual Design - Control ResonantBest Game Expansion - Doom: The Dark Ages Best Indie Game Self-Published - Meccha ChameleonBest Indie Game - Valheim Best Gaming Hardware - Steam Controller Studio of the Year - Capcom Best Early Access Game - Subnautica 2 Best Soundtrack - DispatchStill Playing - Mobile - Balatro Still Playing - Consoles & PC - Minecraft Streamers' Choice - Meccha ChameleonBest Game Trailer - Resident Evil Requiem - Evil Has Always Had A Name Best Remake / Remaster - The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt - Remastered Developers' Choice - Meccha ChameleonBest Game Adaptation - Iron Lung Best Supporting Performer - Grace Saif, Diana, Pragmata Best Lead Performer - Angela Sant'Albano - Grace Ashcroft, Resident Evil Requiem PC Game of the Year - Crimson Desert Console Game of the Year - Resident Evil Requiem Critics' Choice - Big Walk Most Wanted Game - The Witcher 4 Ultimate Game of the Year - Resident Evil Requiem",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T12:35:14.000Z",
